(100878, 'Aberfeldy 18-year-old', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Scotland', 'Whiskey / Whisky', 54.9, '', FALSE, '2025-02-07', 'Single Malt', 18, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://static.whiskybase.com/storage/whiskies/3/4/781/388450-big.jpg'),
(101159, 'Aberfeldy 18-year-old', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Scotland', 'Whiskey / Whisky', 40, '', FALSE, '2025-02-10', 'Single Malt', 18, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://static.whiskybase.com/storage/whiskies/5/5/924/215190-big.jpg'),
(101449, 'Aberfeldy 18-year-old', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Scotland', 'Whiskey / Whisky', 43, 'Hendrick’s wondrous botanical signature consists of flowers, roots, fruits, and seeds from the world over. They function to complement and set the stage for our delicious duet of infusions: rose petal and cucumber. Hendrick’s is the marriage of two different spirits from two rare and unusual stills: the Bennet still and the Carter-Head still. By combining the two, we are able to create an extraordinarily smooth gin that has the required character and balance of subtle flavours. Hendrick''s distills in miniscule batches of 500 litres, which gives our master distiller even greater control of her careful artistry.', FALSE, '2025-01-28', 'Single Malt', 18, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://static.whiskybase.com/storage/whiskies/1/5/9150/290354-big.jpg'),
(100366, 'Hendrick''s Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 44, '', FALSE, '2025-01-08', 'Contemporary', 0, 'https://88bamboo.co/blogs/gin/hendricks-gin-44-abv', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1209/picture?type=normal'),
(100575, 'Monkey 47 Schwarzwald Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Germany', 'Gin', 47, 'Admittedly, it appears somewhat eccentric to claim that a recipe for gin has the power to unite great British traditions, the exoticness of India, and the purity and nativeness of the Black Forest. And yet it is precisely this eccentricity that defines the enigmatic character of Montgomery Collins, from whom our Schwarzwald Dry Gin originates. His childhood as the son of a diplomat in East Asia, his military career among the ruins of Berlin, and his late-adopted home in the Black Forest supply the autobiographical background for a recipe that represents an audacious combination of native Black Forest herbs and berries and exotic Asian botanicals. A good third of the ingredients for this special gin come from the Black Forest and are definitely not what you would call typical gin flavorings!  In total, 47 handpicked ingredients, prepared in extremely soft spring water from our own Black Forest source, give Monkey 47, whose pièce de résistance is the use of local cranberries as some sort of "secret weapon" typical to the Black Forest, its unrivaled complexity and quality, which is fully brought to bear through masterly distillation and maturing in traditional earthenware containers.', FALSE, '2025-01-15', 'Contemporary', 0, 'https://88bamboo.co/blogs/gin/monkey-47-schwarzwald-dry-gin-monkey-47-sloe-gin-side-by-side-tasting', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1597/picture?type=normal'),
(101171, 'Gin Mare', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Spain', 'Gin', 42.7, 'The time had come to show the world what we were capable of and the response has exceeded our wildest expectations. Gin Mare has redefined the concept of Dry Gin with its uniquely Mediterranean character. Using a revolutionary combination of botanicals which includes the Arbequina olive, basil, rosemary and thyme, Gin Mare has managed to distil, bottle and export the very essence of the Mediterranean for which we are so loved and envied: our gastronomy, our way of life, our climate, our land and our sea. The birthplace of civilizations that have set sail to the four corners of the earth to conquer the most demanding and most exquisite of palates.', FALSE, '2025-02-15', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1041/picture?type=normal'),
(100389, 'Bombay Sapphire Distilled London Dry Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 40, 'We are passionate about producing the finest gin possible; which is why the creation of Bombay Sapphire is truly unique. Whilst ordinary gins boil their botanicals directly in the spirit to achieve their flavour, the taste of Bombay Sapphire is created through the Vapour Infusion process. The 10 precious botanicals used in our gin are held separate from the spirit in perforated copper baskets, and when the heated vapours rise, the distinctive flavour of the botanicals are released. The result? A complex aromatic liquid that delivers a broader, more balanced flavour.', FALSE, '2025-02-10', 'London Dry', 0, 'https://88bamboo.co/blogs/gin/bombay-sapphire-london-dry-gin-40-abv-a-gem-of-a-gin', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/460/picture?type=normal'),
(101407, 'The Botanist', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 46, 'An exciting and unusual gin from Islay whisky distillery Bruichladdich, The Botanist is made in a Lomond still christened Ugly Betty and contains no fewer than 31 botanicals, of which 22 are native to the Southern Hebridean island itself. These latter include the likes of mugwort, meadowsweet and the enigmatic Lady''s Bedstraw flowers, and the resultant dry gin is described, perhaps unsurprisingly, as ''floral''.', FALSE, '2025-02-09', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'https://88bamboo.co/blogs/gin/islay-botanist-gin-the-gin-made-by-the-minds-at-bruichladdich-distillery', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2245/picture?type=normal'),
(101033, 'Tanqueray Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 43.1, 'A blend of the purest four-times-distilled spirit and a hand picked selection of four botanicals (juniper, coriander, angelica root and liquorice), London Dry Gin offers uniquely balanced gin experience. Said to have been Frank Sinatra’s preferred gin, London Dry’s edge and sophistication have long made it a favourite with the stars in fashion, film and music. Tanqueray’s iconic bottle design is a contemporary update of the original 1948 design, which in turn, was inspired by the shape of a classic cocktail shaker. The famous Tanqueray family crest embossed on the glass of each bottle features a pineapple, a historic symbol of hospitality and warm welcome.', FALSE, '2025-02-07', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2215/picture?type=normal'),
(101461, 'Brockmans Intensely Smooth Premium Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 40, 'There are various ways of making gin. Brockmans gin is created from a beautiful recipe of botanicals. These naturally grown aromatic botanicals are steeped in pure grain spirit for many hours to release their oils and aromas. Thereafter, Brockmans is distilled in a 100 year old traditional copper still, where we capture the heart of the gin distillation. The distinctive gin notes and the aroma of coriander married with the softer notes of blueberry and blackberry help deliver an exquisite new taste experience and an intensely smooth gin.', FALSE, '2025-02-24', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/526/picture?type=normal'),
(101116, 'Roku Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Japan', 'Gin', 43, 'The Roku Gin incorporates six traditional Japanese botanicals that are infused, distilled and blended by Suntory Spirits in Osaka, Japan, along with eight other botanicals traditionally used in gin. The six Japanese botanicals – Sakura flower, Sakura leaf, Yuzu peel, Sencha tea, Gyokuro tea and Sansho pepper – are harvested in accordance with ‘shun’, the tradition of enjoying each ingredient at its best by only harvesting once it has reached its peak flavour potential and perfection. The six Japanese botanicals are distilled using a selection of different pot stills, each chosen to ensure the best flavour is extracted from each botanical. The result is a complex yet harmonious gin with a smooth and silky texture. Roku''s bottle is cast in a hexagonal shape, representing each Japanese botanical, and is finished with delicate embossing. The Japanese kanji symbol for six is printed on the label, which is made of traditional washi paper and finished with subtle touches of gold.', FALSE, '2025-02-11', 'Contemporary', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/4379/picture?type=normal'),
(100369, 'Bulldog', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 40, 'Bulldog London Dry Gin is not your grandfather''s gin. Bulldog Gin is a multi-award winning, super-premium gin handcrafted at an English distillery that has been making the highest quality gin for over 250 years. The exotic botanicals and high quality ingredients combined with the quadruple distillation process allow our product to defy convention with a balanced flavour and crisp finish. Bulldog is made from Norfolk wheat from the fertile East Anglia region of England, Britain''s purest fresh water from Wales and a distinctive blend of 12 botanicals from 8 countries around the world - Chinese dragon eye, Turkish white poppy seeds, Asian lotus leaves, Italian juniper, Moroccan coriander, German angelica, Spanish lemon, Chinese liquorice, Italian orris, Spanish almonds, Asian cassia and French lavender. We source our botanicals from the same place every year to ensure consistency.', FALSE, '2025-02-01', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/542/picture?type=normal'),
(100348, 'Nordés Atlantic Galician Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Spain', 'Gin', 40, 'Nordés is a gin created by means of a slow, unhurried distillation process. To obtain a wine liqueur, which is the soul of the product, a portion of local Galician grape of the Albariño variety is used. The distilling process is enhanced with the maceration of 12 local and foreign botanical elements. In addition to juniper, it has various native Galician herbs such as lemon verbena, laurel leaves, sage or eucalyptus. It also incorporates salicornia, -a sea plant- cardamom, peppermint, ginger, hibiscus, black Ceylon tea and quinine. This is a highly aromatic gin, with hints of white flowers, lemon verbena and ginger, in harmony with balsamic hints of eucalyptus, laurel and mint. Delicate floral and fruity aromas accompanied by a subtle hint of juniper. Fresh and fruity on the palate, reminiscent of laurel and juniper on the nose.', FALSE, '2025-02-26', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1683/picture?type=normal'),
(100443, 'Opihr London Dry Gin - Spices Of The Orient', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 40, 'The heritage of Opihr Spices of the Orient Gin is firmly rooted in the ancient Spice Route. Traditionally merchants would travel thousands of miles along the route, trading exotic spices and botanicals from distant lands. Opihr Spices of the Orient Gin is crafted with a selection of exotic hand-picked botanicals, carefully chosen by Opihr''s Master Distiller, including spicy Cubeb berries from Indonesia, Black Pepper from India and Coriander from Morocco. The botanicals in Opihr Gin make the journey to their final destination, the oldest distillery in England, where quality gin has been traditionally distilled, using the same London Dry Gin method, since 1761. Here the botanicals are married with fine English spirit to produce an exotic oriental spiced gin. A rich and robust gin with a smooth perfume and sharp bursts of citrus. Key notes of cumin and cardamom provide a warm, earthy background balanced with grapefruit peel. Soft camphor on the palate, some sweetness and Oriental spices create a warm mouth feel that lingers but does not increase intensity.', FALSE, '2025-01-15', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1741/picture?type=normal'),
(100144, 'Tanqueray No. Ten', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 47.3, 'The flagship gin of the 183-year-old distillery, Tanqueray No. 10 is made with handpicked fruit and botanicals, with a delicious hint of juniper and coriander. Distilled under the watchful eye of Tom Nichol, the refined tasting Tanqueray counts numerous celebrity fans, from Snoop Dogg to Rita Ora.', FALSE, '2025-01-14', 'London Dry', 0, 'https://88bamboo.co/blogs/gin/tanqueray-n%C2%BA-ten-gin-47-3-trying-the-stanley-tucci-approved-ultra-premium-tanqueray-gin', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2218/picture?type=normal'),
(100536, 'Tanqueray Flor De Sevilla Distilled Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 41.3, 'The World''s favourite gin has launched a brand new flavour - made with the unique, zesty and bittersweet taste of Seville Oranges. Inspired by an original recipe from Charles Tanqueray, which was in turn inspired by his travels to the sun-soaked groves of Spain in the 1860s. Tanqueray Flor de Sevilla delivers a fruitful and zesty taste that we think is stupidly delicious - they truly have bottled the taste of the sun-soaked Mediterranean in a uniquely enjoyable yet complex gin.', FALSE, '2025-01-24', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/5472/picture?type=normal'),
(100283, 'Drumshanbo Gunpowder Irish Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Ireland', 'Gin', 43, 'It takes an inquisitive, questing spirit to produce the most remarkable results. Through the years PJ Rigney has taken many journeys from the familiar into terra incognita. In time, those travels brought him here, to the wild and unspoilt landscape of Drumshanbo, Co Leitrim. And it was here that his curious mind, filled with the great oriental traditions of distilling fruit, herbs and botanicals, got to work. He created The Shed Distillery of PJ Rigney, with its medieval copper pot stills, and began a quest to fuse oriental botanicals with the local Irish ones. As it turned out, they got on very well indeed. The result of this passionate exploration is Drumshanbo Gunpowder Gin – unique, extraordinary and remarkable as the elusive creature PJ has occasionally glimpsed in the fields, the Drumshanbo Jackalope.', FALSE, '2025-01-26', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1155/picture?type=normal'),
(101109, 'Tanqueray Rangpur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 41.3, 'Tanqueray Rangpur Gin unveils the best kept secret of the British-Indian tradition. The rare Rangpur lime, traditionally used to smooth down the gin, brings an exotic bold flavour to the already perfect combination of juniper, coriander, bay leaves and ginger.', FALSE, '2025-01-05', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2221/picture?type=normal'),
(101264, 'Bobby’s Schiedam Dry Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Netherlands', 'Gin', 42, 'Bobby’s Schiedam Dry Gin is named after my grandfather, Jacobus Alfons, known to his friends and family as Bob or Bobby. It was his recipe that inspired us. It took us almost two years to make Bobby’s, a very fine and balanced distilled gin. Eight botanicals all separately distilled. No additives, sugars or extractions. simply pure taste. A fresh take on a timeless classic. Bobby’s is a unique blend of Indonesian spice and traditional botanicals. Spicy and fragrant on the nose, a fresh burst of citrus and herbals at first sip and with a slight hum of pepper.', FALSE, '2025-02-26', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/449/picture?type=normal'),
(100609, 'Malfy Gin - Con Limone', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Gin', 41, 'Malfy Gin is distilled by the Vergnano family in Moncalieri, Italy using a traditional vacuum still. Malfy Gin’s key botanical additions are lemon peels sourced from the Italian coastline. The lemon peels are steeped in alcohol and pressed in a basket press. The infusion is then blended with the juniper and other botanicals before being distilled in a stainless steel vacuum still. Malfy Gin is perfectly balanced at 41% acc/vol - enough strength to carry the delicious flavours of the botanicals, but not so strong as to be overwhelming. The flavour is deliciously zesty citrus while still maintaining classic complex gin flavours - it is not overwhelming junipery. Malfy is made using Italian grown Juniper and 5 other botanicals. The lemons used in Malfy Gin are sourced from the Italian coastal regions.', FALSE, '2025-02-15', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1512/picture?type=normal'),
(100323, 'Beefeater London Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 40, 'One London distillery, 9 stills and as many botanicals make the world''s most awarded gin under the supervision of the world''s most experienced Master Distiller. A quintessential London dry gin made with big juniper character and strong citrus notes, this is an authentic London Dry for those that enjoy the real taste of gin. Still made in London to our founder James Burrough''s original recipe of 9 botanicals featuring bold juniper, zesty Seville Orange and Lemon Peel, Desmond Payne - the world''s most experienced master distiller - oversees a bold and distinct gin that sets the standard for London Dry Gins and claims the title of The World''s Most Awarded Gin, based on International Spirits Awards from 2004 - 2019. With nearly 200 years of distilling heritage, there was a time when we would hand weigh our botanicals for every batch of Gin we produced...We call it this morning.', FALSE, '2025-02-13', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/329/picture?type=normal'),
(101211, 'Malfy Gin - Rosa', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Gin', 41, 'Italian Juniper, Sicilian Pink Grapefruit, Italian Rhubarb and 5 other botanicals. This bright delicious gin is like no other. Our sun-ripened Sicilian Pink Grapefruits are grown in citrus groves on the Mediterranean coast where the mountains greet the sea. The taste is juicy fresh grapefruit, with a rich long juniper finish. Enjoy this colorful burst of Italian sunshine on the rocks, with tonic or in your favourite cocktail.', FALSE, '2025-01-17', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/5716/picture?type=normal'),
(101433, 'Elephant Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Germany', 'Gin', 45, 'Elephant Gin is an award-winning handcrafted premium gin of 45% alcoholic volume made with rare African botanicals. While its story started in South Africa, Elephant Gin is handmade in Germany with a focus on highest quality production standards. All ingredients are hand-selected, bottles custom-made, labels hand-written and production efforts controlled by working in small batches. The gin’s nose yields a subtle juniper aroma with an undertone of mountain pine and other herbaceous notes. The taste is complex but strikingly smooth, encompassing floral, fruity and spicy flavours. From the very first bottle sold in September 2013, Elephant Gin has been giving 15% of all proceeds to two African elephant foundations to support the preservation of the African wildlife and help ensure that future generations will also be able to explore these magnificent landscapes.', FALSE, '2025-01-02', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/844/picture?type=normal'),
(101119, 'Silent Pool Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 43, 'Silent Pool Gin is a classic gin at heart. It is full-bodied and fresh, with depth, clarity, and above all else flavour. Produced with 24 unique botanicals, Silent Pool Gin is a rich and clean juniper-driven spirit with floral layers of lavender and chamomile. Fresh notes of citrus and kafir lime are grounded with the subtle sweetness of local honey, creating a well-balanced gin that is both traditional and refreshingly individual.', FALSE, '2025-01-02', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2040/picture?type=normal'),
(100030, 'Whitley Neill Original Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 42, 'Whitley Neill is a handcrafted gin of exceptional quality inspired by the vivid beauty and mystery of Africa, and a never-ending drive for perfection. Distilled in small batches by Johnny Neill, a direct descendant of Thomas Greenall and the last in a long line of distillers, Whitley Neill brings together 8 generations of expertise and a life-long love of adventure. The result is an inimitable, award-winning gin that skilfully blends and balances rare African botanicals and unusual aromatics, to create an enigmatic experience to savour.', FALSE, '2025-01-23', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2427/picture?type=normal'),
(100354, 'Whitley Neill Rhubarb & Ginger Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 43, 'Whitley Neill Rhubarb & Ginger Gin is inspired by the glory of a traditional English country garden. Alongside Whitley Neill''s signature botanical, the Baobab fruit, this gin is infused with the essence of rhubarb and extracts of real ginger. Building on a smooth base of English gin, the rhubarb brings a tart crispness to the palate, while the ginger gives it a spicy, warming character.', FALSE, '2025-01-30', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/4258/picture?type=normal'),
(100009, 'Martin Miller''s Dry Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 40, 'Martin Miller''s makes two types of gin. The original 80 proof (40abv) was the first to be developed back in 1998 and was launched in 1999 making it the original Super Premium Gin. Made to a traditional London Dry Style in flavour profile and dryness, this gin uses a mix of ultra traditional distilling methods allied to Martin''s own iconoclastic ''take'' on gin distilling. In a break with tradition, there are two separate distillations for the juniper and earthier botanicals that are later ''married'' or blended with a second separate distillation of the citrus elements of bitter orange peel from Seville, lemon and lime peel. These techniques contribute to the gin''s unique freshness and clarity of flavour.', FALSE, '2025-01-18', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1531/picture?type=normal'),
(101190, 'Caorunn Small Batch Scottish Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 41.8, 'Caorunn is a small batch, quadruple-distilled Scottish Gin personally crafted by one man – our Gin Master, Simon Buley. Using only the finest pure grain spirit, natural Scottish Water and 11 botanical gin ingredients, he personally crafts each and every bottle of Caorunn. Caorunn is the taste of wild sophistication – an expert infusion of five locally foraged with six traditional botanicals. Beautifully versatile, Caorunn is perfect in any classic or contemporary cocktail.', FALSE, '2025-01-22', 'Contemporary', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/590/picture?type=normal'),
(100393, 'Gordon''s Premium Pink Distilled Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 37.5, 'Inspired by an original Gordon’s recipe from the 1880s, the pink gin is perfectly crafted to balance the refreshing taste of Gordon’s with the natural sweetness of raspberries and strawberries, with the tang of redcurrant served up in a unique blushing tone. Made using only natural fruit flavours to guarantee the highest quality real berry taste.', FALSE, '2025-02-07', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/4299/picture?type=normal'),
(100504, 'Le Tribute Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Spain', 'Gin', 43, 'MG Destilerías has been in the business since 1835 and launched its first gin in 1940. The fourth generation wanted to leverage in the family’s know how to create a completely renovated liquid and impactful design coming up with Le Tribute Gin. As the family also started to produce non-alcoholic beverages in the late 80’s, Le Tribute Tonic Water has arisen as a challenge to their knowledge in the mixers category production, perfectly combining with the gin. Le Tribute Gin is made with the best quality wheat and barley alcohol base. After the handmade selection of the botanicals (juniper, lemongrass, orange, lemon, coriander, grapefruit, kumquat, tangerine and lime) there is another filter made at our Distillery, before hand-peeling and macerating, resulting in a fresh gin, yet dry enough.', FALSE, '2025-02-01', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/3006/picture?type=normal'),
(101236, 'Gin Sul', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Germany', 'Gin', 43, 'Gin Sul is produced in the distillery Altonaer Spirituosen Manufaktur and exudes the unique aromas of labdanum, which is a plant found at the west coast of Portugal. You will also detect the typical notes of fine juniper, rosemary, rose blossoms and lemon peel. The gin is filled into bottles of white clay that keep the drink safe from incidence of light and temperature fluctuation. When you drink it with a nice tonic water, ice cubes and a lemon peel zest, you will experience the special feeling of Saudade - a Portuguese equivalent of nostalgic yearning, which Gin Sul celebrates to its fullest!', FALSE, '2025-02-20', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1050/picture?type=normal'),
(100872, 'Bloom', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 40, 'Bloom Gin is a floral London Dry Gin, inspired by nature. Master Distiller Joanne Moore, the world’s first female gin Master Distiller, chose the flowers of chamomile and honeysuckle, with the citrus fruit pomelo, to make up the three main botanicals for Bloom – each one contributing to the delicate gin drinking experience.', FALSE, '2025-02-22', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/436/picture?type=normal'),
(100509, 'Gordon''s London Dry Gin - Export', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 37.5, 'Not long after we started bottling in green glass in the early 1900''s, we had our first big order of Gordon''s to be sent to Australia! To mark the occasion we designed a new export label and fitted it to the green bottle. However, it looked overly bold for a gin with serious credentials so it was paired with clear glass and the export bottle was born.', FALSE, '2025-01-05', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/4298/picture?type=normal'),
(101466, 'Isle Of Harris Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 45, 'While preparations continue for distilling the spirit for ''The Hearach'' whisky, our distillers are busy creating The Isle of Harris Gin. The small copper still, known affectionally as ''The Dottach'', imbues our spirit with the complex delights of nine specially chosen botanicals as we seek to capture the elemental nature of our island, particularly the maritime influences of the seas which surround us on all sides. Juniper, coriander, angelica root, orris root, cubebs, bitter orange peel, licorice and cassia bark all play their role in defining the taste of our gin. But it is sugar kelp which is key to the subtle coastal notes that mark out our spirit. Hand-harvested by a local diver from the deep underwater forests of the Outer Hebrides, this natural and sustainanable ingredient completes the wider aspects of the gin''s flavour profile.', FALSE, '2025-01-17', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1286/picture?type=normal'),
(100088, 'Gordon''s London Dry Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 37.5, 'Gordon''s London Dry gin is carefully distilled using a secret recipe. The distinctively refreshing taste comes from the finest handpicked juniper berries and a selection of other botanicals. It''s the taste that''s made Gordon''s the world''s best-selling London Dry gin. In the UK, Gordon''s is sold in a green bottle. In the rest of the world, Gordon''s has a yellow label.', FALSE, '2025-01-10', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1115/picture?type=normal'),
(100097, 'Jinzu Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 41.3, 'Jinzu combines typical Gin botanicals with exotic botanicals from Japan. That is, Juniper from Tuscany and coriander from East Europe, and Japanese botanicals, yuzu citrus and cherry blossom. Now, where the magic happens, is in the inclusion of distilled Junmai sake. This is where the East meets the West and where, for the first time, two national treasures (Gin & Sake) come together in fusion.', FALSE, '2025-02-15', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1316/picture?type=normal'),
(100713, 'Copperhead London Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Belgium', 'Gin', 40, 'In the eye of the storm, when gin & tonic suddenly became thé aperitif of the famous, the foodies and eventually just you and me, Copperhead hit the market hard by swimming against the stream. Where all the competitors were making Western Dry gins, Copperhead returned to the roots of gin and created a London Dry gin. Many ingredients were listed as options to create the ultimate gin and after a month-long process experimenting with different batches, they found the perfect balance of 5 ingredients. The first Copperhead gin was born and it was named Copperhead London Dry Gin, or The Original.', FALSE, '2025-01-18', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/667/picture?type=normal'),
(100629, 'Berliner Brandstifter - Berlin Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Germany', 'Gin', 43.3, 'Guided by the vision of creating a gin that would embody the spirit of Berlin, Berliner Brandstifter extended its product range in 2013 and launched the Berlin Dry Gin. An experience for the senses, each bottle of gin takes you on a journey through the city’s sunniest days; elderflowers in full bloom, delicate mallow growing in the fields, the sweet scent of woodruff in the air that surprises you on a stroll through the woods. The fresh taste of Berliner Brandstifter Gin is like taking a wonderful walk on a careless summer day in the capital. Each year, the botanicals and herbs used for the production and refinement of the fine distillate Berlin Dry Gin are cultivated and handpicked on the Berliner Speisegut farm in Gatow. The same high-quality 7fold filtered wheat distillate alcohol base is used for the gin, as for the production of the Kornbrand. The wheat is of the highest quality class and grown exclusively in Germany. All the ingredients for the Berlin Dry Gin are carefully combined by our partner who inspects each bottle individually. The production is limited to 9,999 bottles annually, due to the small harvest volume. Bottling and numbering are done attentively, by hand. This guarantees that every drop of gin comes from a precious place, is produced in a loving environment and thus brings a unique character to the glass. The foundation of the gin’s strong character lies in the juniper. The flavour is perfectly rounded off with a hint of fresh blossoms and a unique freshness. It carefully balances smooth, soft and flowery nuances with the complex and refined foundation of a classic gin. The floral notes harmonize perfectly with the sophisticated juniper aromas.', FALSE, '2025-02-17', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/366/picture?type=normal'),
(101343, 'Citadelle Gin De France - Original', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Gin', 44, 'Citadelle Original is our very first gin, the French gin par excellence. Dry and structured, it strikes a perfect balance between finesse and intensity. It has been the signature expression of our savoir-faire since 1996. Citadelle Original offers a rich and complete aromatic palette. Juniper introduces Citadelle’s signature botanical from the outset, then opens up to bright citrus notes that enhances the juniper berry’s freshness. The finish leans more exotic… long and spicy thanks to touches of pepper, nutmeg and cinnamon.', FALSE, '2025-01-14', 'Contemporary', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/627/picture?type=normal'),
(101068, 'G''Vine Floraison', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Gin', 40, 'Adored by neophytes and connoisseurs alike. Fresh, smooth, rounded and vibrantly floral. G''Vine Floraison captures the splendour of the vineyards end of spring, when the vine flowers'' enchanting aroma fills the air for a few fleeting days as it blossoms. Its distinctive and refreshing style lends itself to make a simply sublime gin&tonic. While most gins are made from grain, G''Vine is made from the noble and smooth grape spirit, as were the very first historical juniper spirits back in the 13th century. It is a smooth and sophisticated canvas for a fine selection of 10 botanicals gently distilled in individual batches, including juniper berries, green cardamom, ginger roots and the exclusive vine flower.', FALSE, '2025-02-05', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/969/picture?type=normal'),
(100466, 'Aviation American Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Gin', 42, 'Aviation belongs to an entirely new category of dry gins. These gins embody a shift away from the usual overabundance of juniper toward a more forward balance of botanicals. Aviation explores the rich, floral and savory notes of lavender, cardamom, and sarsaparilla to capture the lushness, spice, creativity, and freshness of the Pacific Northwest. In this way, we offer the American palate its first real taste of American gin.', FALSE, '2025-01-05', 'Contemporary', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/264/picture?type=normal'),
(100618, 'Plymouth Original Strength', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 41.2, 'Plymouth Original Strength is a unique, protected style of gin originating from the city of Plymouth, South West England. Since 1793 it has been distilled from a unique blend of 7 botanicals, soft Dartmoor water and pure grain alcohol at the historic Black Friars Distillery - the oldest working distillery in England', FALSE, '2025-01-22', 'Plymouth Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1830/picture?type=normal'),
(100533, 'Hendrick''s Midsummer Solstice Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 43.4, 'This delightful and refreshing take on the Hendrick''s house style gin is Master Distiller Lesley''s Gracie''s tribute to the sensory powers of the Midsummer Solstice, when botanicals (flowers in particular) are believed to be at their most powerful. It sees the Hendrick''s Gin recipe instilled with a secretive selection of floral essences that enhance its existing botanical bouquet. The result is an enchantingly floral gin that blossoms on the palate, but is unmistakably Hendrick''s. This especially unique gin is true to the Hendrick''s original ''round'' house style, but is infused with floral essences that capture the aromatic intensity of a midsummer day.  On the nose, juniper adorned to perfection with fragrant zest and deeply floral character. Initial brightness melts to reveal deep undertones of orange blossom and an alluring exotic ripeness. On the palate, a bloom of lush flora melts to reveal the unmistakable Hendrick''s House style; juniper, subtle spice, and a mellow floral finish which luxuriates on the palate eventually giving way to the signature rose whisper.', FALSE, '2025-02-15', 'Contemporary', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/6257/picture?type=normal'),
(100355, 'Ungava Canadian Premium Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Canada', 'Gin', 43.1, 'Its particular aroma can be traced back to six rare botanicals, native to the Arctic region, from which it is made. Handpicked in the wild during the fleeting summer season, then infused the traditional way, they are handcrafted into an authentic gin with a unique taste to the delight of adventurous amateurs and connoisseurs alike.', FALSE, '2025-02-03', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2334/picture?type=normal'),
(100902, 'Malfy Gin - Con Arancia', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Gin', 41, 'A fruity firework with well-coordinated botanicals. The most important ingredient, the Sicilian blood orange peel, is macerated in distilled alcohol for 36 hours together with Italian juniper berries. This gives the Malfy Gin con Arancia its beautiful ruby ​​red color. In a second distillation step, the infusion is distilled with 7 different botanicals in a vacuum still and brought to 41% vol by addition of crystal clear spring water.', FALSE, '2025-01-15', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/5411/picture?type=normal'),
(101527, 'The London No. 1 - Original Blue Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom / Spain', 'Gin', 47, 'It is all of the components that give The London No 1 it''s singular character - the quality of the ingredients, the distillation method, the colour and the bottle''s design. Distilled in small batches in the heart of London, this gin''s unique flavour is the result of the quality of the raw ingredients used, as well as its distillation in Pot Stills (traditionally the only stills used for distillation in small quantities). During the 18th century, London was a world-renowned hub for international trade, where all types of herbs and spices were bought and sold. That is why the London Gin soon became the most complex drink on the market. Loyal to this tradition, The London Nº1 consists of 12 different botanicals from around the world. Twelve carefully chosen ingredients that create a unique gin, giving it a unique complexity, elegance and perfect balance. To the traditional juniper, coriander and angelica are added lemon peel, cassia bar, liquorice, cinnamon, almond, savory, iris root, orange peel and bergamot.', FALSE, '2025-02-16', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2257/picture?type=normal'),
(100976, 'The Illusionist Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Germany', 'Gin', 45, 'Warm aromas of juniper, nutmeg, licorice and angelica, notes of lavender and rosemary and nuances of fresh lemons and oranges dominate this Dry Gin. The bottom line: A blue flower from the other end of the world that your Illusionist in a deep blue you versetzt.Willst the true face of this experience Gins, then mix your illusionist with a tonic or other fruity mixed drinks. He turns, showing his gentle face and changes its color in a soft pink.', FALSE, '2025-02-13', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2975/picture?type=normal'),
(100543, 'Ableforth''s Bathtub Gin - (Formerly Professor Cornelius Ampleforth''s Bathtub Gin)', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 43.3, 'A multi award-winning gin which is made using a traditional method known as cold compounding. Botanicals such as juniper, coriander, cardamom, cassia, orange peel and clove are infused in top quality copper pot-still spirit, resulting in Bathtub Gin’s extraordinary flavour as well as its handsome tint. Think of it as the ‘dry-hopping’ of gin. Each bottle is wrapped entirely by hand using paper, twine and wax. A favourite amongst amateur and professional mixologists alike, Bathtub Gin is also absolutely perfect in a classic Gin & Tonic.', FALSE, '2025-01-13', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1861/picture?type=normal'),
(100049, 'Brooklyn Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Gin', 40, 'Brooklyn Gin is a craft spirit made in New York with fresh citrus peels and hand-cracked juniper. Our gin is fresh, complex, and flavorful. It’s good enough to drink on its own and we’re proud of that. We use 100% fresh citrus peels and hand-cracked juniper. By hand-cutting the citrus fruit, and releasing the essential oils in the juniper berries, we make a more vibrant gin than the distillers who use frozen or dried citrus peels. We use one Christian Carl copper pot still. We take three days to make 300 bottles of gin. Unlike mass-produced factory gins, we do everything by hand. It takes more time and effort, but we believe you can taste it in your very first sip. In kinship with the craftsmen who embody the Brooklyn spirit – we set out to make a small-batch American gin by hand. We distill Brooklyn Gin using locally purchased fruit and 100% corn grown in upstate New York.', FALSE, '2025-02-04', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/535/picture?type=normal'),
(100881, 'Sipsmith London Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 41.6, 'A particularly dry gin with a zesty, citrus finish. The quintessential expression of a classic, traditional London Dry Gin. Bold, complex and aromatic – smooth enough for a Martini, but rich and balanced, perfect for a G&T.', FALSE, '2025-01-03', 'London Dry', 0, 'https://88bamboo.co/blogs/gin/sipsmith-london-dry-gin-vs-sipsmith-v-j-o-p-a-battle-of-the-london-drys', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2054/picture?type=normal'),
(100494, 'Needle Blackforest Distilled Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Germany', 'Gin', 40, 'A classical Gin carries a bit of British, Dutch, Spanish and, of course, German history. The convincing and unique taste of a Black Forest Gin, like Needle, is not only the combination of classic Gins, but also the love given by the Black Forest master distillers. Needle is the special Black Forest experience. The logo reflects the so-called “common spruce” (Picea abies), which gives the Needle a special touch and distinctive aroma. During a walk in the beautiful Black Forest of Baden, it is this unique smell of spruce needles that makes a day recreative and exciting and at the same time. It’s precisely this experience that is revealed to the connoisseur when removing the real wood cork of the Needle and when getting spoiled with 10 impressive Botanicals. The green pharmacy bottle conceals a distillate based on aromatic juniper berries. Besides flowery lavender in accordance with the typical pungency of ginger characterize the taste. Furthermore the Needle indulges with a citrus note of sun-ripened lemons and oranges of best quality. A touch of orient is attached by the addition of pimento and cinnamon. But it’s the hand-picked spruce needles, which give the Needle his name and unmistakable character. Needle is Black Forest. Needle is all you need.', FALSE, '2025-02-21', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/3591/picture?type=normal'),
(100714, 'Harahorn Norwegian Small Batch Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Norway', 'Gin', 46, 'The Harahorn. For many centuries, hunters and mountain men have sworn to have seen it. In North American folklore this creature is known as Jackalope; in Norway we know it as the Harahorn. Harahorn is also the name of a Norwegian Mountain. From that mountain plateau, beneath the northern lights, we found the wonderful juniper berries for our Norwegian Gin. We traced the Harahorn’s tracks through abandoned mountain farms where we found our rhubarb, to the deep forests of the Norwegian Lowlands where we harvest our blueberries and you will have our handcrafted small batch gin. Fresh, clean flavors of juniper, fruit and spices. Clean aroma, fine notes of juniper and citrus. Botanicals include juniper berries, blueberries, rhubarb, seaweed, angelica root, wild marjoram and many more.', FALSE, '2025-02-22', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1177/picture?type=normal'),
(101273, 'Ferdinand''s Saar Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Germany', 'Gin', 44, 'Carefully hand-picked Riesling grapes from the steep shale slopes of the Zilliken estate on the grand Saarburger Rausch site make our gin a unique taste experience. The craftsmanship of our Master Distiller Andreas Vallendar and over 30 finely balanced botanicals taken from the vineyards and our own cultivation guarantee a high-quality product from the Saar region that promises supreme drinking pleasure.', FALSE, '2025-02-27', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/884/picture?type=normal'),
(101267, 'Siegfried Rheinland Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Germany', 'Gin', 41, 'Siegfried Rheinland Dry Gin is a product from the Rhine Region and a classic Dry Gin: a defined taste but subtle enough to delight with his weighted composition of 18 fine botanicals, his charm and his straight character. On the nose, gentle citrus notes of bitter orange are accompanied by hints of thyme , cardamom and juniper and thus develop a harmonious complexity. On the tongue, the freshness of lavender meets spicy- earthy notes of ginger, angelica root and is finished with a subtle, warm character of linden blooms. Driven by the sheer desire for honest and artisan products we have developed this premium gin. Siegfried is traditionally distilled in small units from only the finest ingredients, without any industrial tools, artificial flavors or additives, with calm, patience and attention to detail.', FALSE, '2025-01-17', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2036/picture?type=normal'),
(100628, 'Knut Hansen Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Germany / South Africa', 'Gin', 42, 'The Hamburg sailor Knut Hansen is the face of our gins. An honest guy who had not let himself be stopped by anybody on his journey, took the liberty of stepping up the places he had always wanted to see, and had a myriad of adventures. We follow exactly from which cultivation the individual ingredients originate in our Knut Hansen Dry Gin. We also place great importance on using North German botanicals. Therefore, we also tell you the origins of our main cultivations: the juniper grows in the Lüneburg Heath, the apples are from the Old Country and the basil as well as the cucumbers we can take lovingly from the familigenigen greenhouse. Knut Hansen Dry Gin is produced with a lot of love for the detail in the Dolleruper Destille near Flensburg on a copper 200l distillery of the company Arnold Holstein. In an elaborate process, we distill our gin four times with extremely slow energy supply and in small passages - only in this way is it possible for us to preserve the unique Knut Hansen flavor and protect the natural flavors in our gin. Finally we fill our finished Knut Hansen Gin by hand into our unmistakable Steinzeugflaschen.', FALSE, '2025-01-13', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/4829/picture?type=normal'),
(100396, 'Edinburgh Rhubarb & Ginger Gin Liqueur', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 20, 'Inspired by our families in every taste, you’ll find pudding at a noisy kitchen table, fruit-picking on a summer’s day, or the nostalgia of an old fashioned sweet shop. Wonder-filled memories, bottled. All of our gin liqueurs are made using the heart of our range, our Classic London Dry. Aromatic lemongrass and lavender balance the warmth of the ginger and sweetness of the rhubarb to create something extraordinary. A sweet, highly perfumed, rhubarb-filled aroma on the nose followed by bright sweetness and a sharp tang, balanced with a pop of citrus on the palate. You’re left with a lingering warmth from the ginger, warm sweet and comfortingly familiar.', FALSE, '2025-02-14', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/837/picture?type=normal'),
(101118, 'Bombay Dry Gin - The Original', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 40, 'Based on a 1761 recipe, at the heart of Bombay Dry Gin is its unique distillation process, vapour infusion. Unlike many other gins, which boil their botanicals directly in the spirit, the 8 exotic botanicals in Bombay Dry Ginare hand placed in a perforated copper basket. The spirit vapour passes through the copper basket infusing the spirit with the aromatic flavours of the botanicals. This way Bombay Dry Gin acquires a subtle yet full flavour taste which makes it such a rounded and distinctive gin.', FALSE, '2025-02-12', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/458/picture?type=normal'),
(100495, 'Mom - God Save The Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom / Spain', 'Gin', 39.5, 'A Premium gin made with red berries and exotic botanical ingredients to achieve its smooth character. Its exciting personality is the result of infusing it after four distillations. Made and bottled in Great Britain. Its unique softness, vibrant red fruit taste and smooth finish are obtained after a careful production process.', FALSE, '2025-01-05', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1590/picture?type=normal'),
(101406, 'Whitley Neill Blood Orange Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 43, 'Blood Orange Gin offers a refreshing, intense orange aroma, hints of liquorice and coriander, and a smooth finish.', FALSE, '2025-02-21', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/5243/picture?type=normal'),
(101426, 'Amuerte Coca Leaf Gin - Black Edition', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Belgium', 'Gin', 43, 'Long before the days of Pablo Escobar and Colombian drug lords, the coca plant held a mystical, powerful role to the people who grew them. In ancient Peruvian society, the coca’s leaves were prized throughout the Incan Empire, treasured for its abilities to fight hunger and illness.  It took just one chance encounter – a coca leaf chewing ceremony with an indigenous tribe, during a backpacking trip through the rainforest – to bring our founders face to face with the mystical flavors of the coca leaf. Our founders were well suited to transform the coca leaf’s flavors into a gin unlike any other. Between the two of us, we bring a 112 year, 4th generation family history of gin distilling, and an unbridled passion for gin. The result? An incredibly well-balanced, lively combination of subtle, bitter coca, with bright notes of tamarillo, papaya, and South American dragon fruit.  And our premium gin is held in the bottle it deserves. Its premium design, created by some of the industry’s most revered designers, is finished with real 24K gold leaf.', FALSE, '2025-01-04', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/5126/picture?type=normal'),
(101203, 'Kyrö Napue Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Finland', 'Gin', 46.3, 'Our rye-based Napue gin boasts locally foraged fresh botanicals, including sea buckthorn, cranberries and birch leaves. The distinct fragrance and flavour of an early morning, misty Finnish meadow is instantly recognisable. Herbal and sweet, essential oils of meadowsweet and gentle citrus on the nose. Full bodied herbal flavour ending with notes of pepper of rye on the tongue.', FALSE, '2025-01-16', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1639/picture?type=normal'),
(100190, 'Sipsmith House Of Commons London Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 40.7, 'Handcrafted exclusively for the House of Commons, our brand new distillation is nothing short of an ode to the historic Acts that have helped gin blossom into what it is today. But this isn’t just a vestige from the past: instead, we’ve added our own Sipsmithian flair to the recipes of the era, serving up a London Dry style that boasts deep juniper notes and a heavenly citrus finish. A toast, then, to the House of Commons – long may gin reign in Westminster!', FALSE, '2025-01-17', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/3521/picture?type=normal'),
(101514, 'Mombasa Club Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 41.5, 'Mombasa Club Gin was inspired by the eponymous private social club on the Kenyan coast, opposite island of Zanzibar, which imported a gin from England for consumption by its members. Distilled four times and the botanicals include angelica root, cassia bark and coriander seeds. A spicy gin with a hint of sweetness.', FALSE, '2025-01-14', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1591/picture?type=normal'),
(100787, 'The Duke Munich Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Germany', 'Gin', 45, 'A noble product starts with the selection of its ingredients. So The Duke Gin is made from purely biological raw materials. The full-bodied aromas of untreated juniper berries have made the difference. Added to this are coriander, lemon peel, angelica root, ginger, lavender flowers, kubeben pepper and other "drugs", so that a total of 13 selected herbs and spices make up this gin. As a typical Bavarian provenance, two botanicals emphasize its place of origin: hop flowers and malt.', FALSE, '2025-01-14', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2248/picture?type=normal'),
(100637, 'Windspiel Premium Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Germany', 'Gin', 47, 'The heart of this creation is the spirit of discovery. It drove Fridericus Rex to bring the potato to Germany and inspired us to produce a gin from it. Classic juniper berries, lemons and coriander combined with our potatoes cultivated in rich volcanic soil result in a traditional gin aroma with a mild, delicate flavour. To give it a special character, cinnamon bark and lavender as well as other botanicals have been added – according to a secret recipe of the master distiller. Dedicated to the great passion of Fridericus Rex: “Windspiel“ (the greyhound).', FALSE, '2025-01-03', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2456/picture?type=normal'),
(101182, 'Bareksten Botanical Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Norway', 'Gin', 46, 'Norwegian herbs, potatoes and berries fight an intense, slow and never-ending battle in extreme environments. Only the strongest and most stubborn survive. Norwegian ingredients, touched only by nature, form the basis for the raw flavours of Bareksten’s botanical spirits.', FALSE, '2025-02-09', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/3686/picture?type=normal'),
(101256, 'Beefeater 24', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 45, 'A sophisticated blend of fine botanicals and exotic teas. 12 hand-selected Botanicals, steeped in London for 24 hours to create a richer and more sophisticated gin. Inspired by aspects of modern london that are simultaneously exhilarating and refined. Beefeater 24 takes a complex blend of 12 botanicals including grapefruit peel and Japanese and Chinese Green Teas, and infuses them in spirit for 24 hours. After distillation, I select the perfect cut, resulting in a London dry gin with a fresh flavour profile that is best enjoyed in modern cocktails. I proudly present Beefeater 24 - a Gin made in London for exciting cities around the world.', FALSE, '2025-02-28', 'London Dry', 0, 'https://88bamboo.co/blogs/gin/beefeater-24-gin-a-beefed-up-london-dry-made-with-japanese-sencha', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/340/picture?type=normal'),
(101110, 'Portobello Road No. 171 Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 42, 'This gin was released by the award-wining Notting Hill bar, Portobello Star, home of the Ginsitute. This is a place where one can learn an awful lot about gin, so you would expect Portobello Road No. 171 to be rather good, and indeed it is. It''s an old-style London Dry Gin, containing traditional botanicals and spices, that harks back to the gins of yesteryear.', FALSE, '2025-02-02', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1844/picture?type=normal'),
(100904, 'Cotswolds Dry Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 46, 'Our Cotswolds Dry Gin has a delectable blend of nine carefully-considered botanicals. The expression of the traditional London dry style comes from the maceration into our pure wheat spirit of juniper, coriander and angelica root, which have been left for 12 hours to allow their flavour characteristics to fully infuse. We then add our unique botanical mix of Cotswolds lavender and bay leaf, grapefruit, lime, black pepper and cardamom seed into our carter head still for distillation before finishing with naturally refined Cotswolds water. The result is a classic well-balanced juniper-led gin with crisp citrus and spice.', FALSE, '2025-02-28', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/689/picture?type=normal'),
(100903, 'Adnams Copper House Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 40, 'Voted the World''s Best Gin at the International Wine & Spirits Competition 2013, our aromatic gin is bursting with juniper, fresh lemon and orange notes as well as warming hints of anise. Adnams from grain to glass, our Copper House Gin is distilled from East Anglian malted barley at our artisan distillery in Southwold. Our copper pot stills are handmade and create a wonderfully flavoursome spirit. This smooth, rich spirit is then redistilled with six carefully chosen botanicals to impart their distinctive aromas and flavours.', FALSE, '2025-02-08', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/139/picture?type=normal'),
(101398, 'Ki No Bi Kyoto Dry Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Japan', 'Gin', 45.7, 'Ki No Bi (‘The Beauty of the Seasons’) is inspired by tradition and is distilled, blended and bottled in Kyoto. Our gin is made in a recognisable dry style but with a distinct Japanese accent. Ki No Bi Kyoto Dry Gin is created with Japanese botanicals such as yellow yuzu from the north of Kyoto Prefecture, hinoki wood chips (Japanese cypress), bamboo, gyokuro tea from the Uji region and green sanshō (Japanese peppercorn) berries.', FALSE, '2025-02-13', 'Contemporary', 0, 'https://88bamboo.co/blogs/features/inside-a-ki-no-bi-gin-masterclass-tasting-the-six-distillates-that-make-up-japan-s-first-craft-gin?srsltid=AfmBOood3aOyqSlriWfCQ0m7bYJx6wvml2zGR9YJLb4vWcV3B08e3UPO', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/3190/picture?type=normal'),
(101503, 'Star Of Bombay', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 47.5, 'Bombay Sapphire introduces Star Of Bombay, a new, super premium small batch gin, slowly distilled to create a spirit of extraordinary beauty. Produced in small batches entirely at the Bombay Sapphire Distillery, Laverstoke Mill, Hampshire, England. Gently dried Bergamot orange peel from the mountains of Calabria, Southern Italy, provides a fragrant, rich citrus note; while the floral musk of ambrette seeds from the tropical yellow hibiscus flower grown in Ecuador, supply a graceful elegance, lifting the precious botanicals at the heart of all Bombay gins to a new dimension. In addition to the added botanicals, the elegant liquid captured in each bottle is created by slowing down the signature Vapour Infusion process to increase the level of extraction from the botanicals, building richer aromas and more intense flavours. The character and complexity of Star Of Bombay allow the liquid to be savoured neat or over ice.', FALSE, '2025-02-05', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2159/picture?type=normal'),
(100641, 'Tarquin''s Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 42, 'A contemporary take on a classic London Dry, we use fragrant handpicked Devon violets and fresh orange zest to deliver an aromatic sensation unlike any other. We like to think the result is comparable to stumbling upon a beautiful orange blossom in the middle of a crisp, dry pine forest. Only the best and most pure spirit (the heart) makes it into Tarquin’s Gin, which is diluted to bottling strength at 42% with Cornish spring water.', FALSE, '2025-02-03', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2223/picture?type=normal'),
(101305, 'Dancing Sands Dry Gin - (Also known as Sacred Spring Dry Gin)', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'New Zealand', 'Gin', 44, 'Sourced from the aquifer that feeds the clearest spring in the world, our gin is double distilled and vapor infused with 8 carefully selected botanicals. The Manuka leaves are picked fresh from our distiller''s farm. Our methods hope to deliver a classic, timeless gin with a contemporary New Zealand twist. Nature''s finest. Pure and simple. Our water is drawn from the aquifier that feeds Golden Bay''s Te Waikoropupu Springs (The Place of the Dancing Sands), the clearest spring in the world, which has an optical clarity measured to 63 metres. A highly aromatic nose, bursting with green manuka leaves and juniper. Balanced on the palate, fragrant undertones of cardamom and Indian spices with a long liquourice tail. Crafted to challenge the gin aficionado. Outside of New Zealand and Australia, Sacred Spring Gin is known as Dancing Sands Gin.', FALSE, '2025-01-23', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/3326/picture?type=normal'),
(100604, 'Warner Edward''s Harrington Victoria''s Rhubarb Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 40, 'Our most regal gin with real provenance, made using a crop of rhubarb that was originally grown in the kitchen gardens of Buckingham Palace during the reign of Queen Victoria, and has since had quite a journey. Half of the crop was sent to the Vice Regal Lodge in Dublin, which later became the President’s House. It has now made its way back to Crown Estate land in Lincolnshire, and is being organically grown by Fraser M Key. The remaining half left in the grounds of Buckingham Palace was destroyed during The War, which makes our rhubarb very special indeed. A wonderful British spicy gin with a dominating and robust rhubarb taste. We use our Harrington Dry Gin with 11 botanicals; angelica root, black pepper, cardamom, cinnamon, coriander seed, dried elderflower, ground nutmeg, juniper, lemon peel, orange peel and one secret ingredient as the base for our Victoria’s Rhubarb Gin.', FALSE, '2025-02-27', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2403/picture?type=normal'),
(100548, 'Edinburgh Classic London Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 43, 'Our Classic gin is an unmistakable London Dry, born in the ancient and magical city of Edinburgh. Much like its birthplace, what lies within this bottle is far from ordinary. The finest grain spirit is brought together with an original balance of 14 botanicals. The woody hint of pine buds, aromatic lemongrass and floral lavender are all present. Fruity jammy flavour from black mulberries balances perfectly with the citrus from the orange and lime peels in the finish. Hazelnuts, thick with natural oils, add texture and a smooth mouthfeel. Perfectly balanced – refreshing, crisp and versatile. The heart of our range, and, in our opinion, the perfect London Dry.', FALSE, '2025-02-05', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/835/picture?type=normal'),
(100971, 'Hernö Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Sweden', 'Gin', 40.5, 'Hernö Gin is a round and smooth London dry gin, with a juniper caracter, fresh citrus notes and a floral complexity which makes the gin very enjoyable on its own. All our gins a one-shot-gins, only diluted with water, from own well, and not chill filtered. We use eight carefully selected botanicals from around the world to make our award winning Hernö Gin. All certified organic. Juniper berries from Hungary, coriander seeds from Bulgaria, lemon that we peel by hand, lingon berries from Sweden, meadowsweet from the United Kingdom, black pepper from India, cassia from Indonesia and fresh vanilla from Madagascar.', FALSE, '2025-01-19', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1222/picture?type=normal'),
(100320, 'Tanqueray Dry Gin Export Strength', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 47.3, 'A blend of the purest four-times-distilled spirit and a hand picked selection of four botanicals (juniper, coriander, angelica root and liquorice), London Dry Gin offers uniquely balanced gin experience. Said to have been Frank Sinatra’s preferred gin, London Dry’s edge and sophistication have long made it a favourite with the stars in fashion, film and music. Tanqueray’s iconic bottle design is a contemporary update of the original 1948 design, which in turn, was inspired by the shape of a classic cocktail shaker. The famous Tanqueray family crest embossed on the glass of each bottle features a pineapple, a historic symbol of hospitality and warm welcome.', FALSE, '2025-02-05', 'London Dry', 0, 'https://88bamboo.co/blogs/gin/tanqueray-london-dry-gin-export-strength-47-3-abv', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2216/picture?type=normal'),
(100232, 'No. 3 London Dry Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom / Netherlands', 'Gin', 46, 'No.3 is the London Dry Gin distilled to a proprietary recipe of Berry Bros. & Rudd, London’s oldest wine and spirit merchant. The name No.3 refers to the address in St James’s Street, London: our home since 1698. No.3 was created to be the last word in gin for a Dry Martini. With juniper at its heart, it unashamedly celebrates the integrity and character of a classic London Dry Gin: six perfectly balanced botanicals distilled in traditional copper pot stills.', FALSE, '2025-02-18', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1676/picture?type=normal'),
(100067, 'Boar Blackforest Premium Dry Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Germany', 'Gin', 43, 'Pure, hand-picked Black Forest herbs are combined in this masterly composition - accentuated by essences of the rare Black Forest Golds - the Black Forest truffles. Light juniper and lavender spikes are harbingers of a composition that unfolds mild taste and eye weighed in flavor, especially through the Indulgence Variation in the midtones full, enriched by the diversity of the minerals Black Forest deep spring water. The mystical moments of pleasure and tangible purity of unspoiled nature give this gin an unprecedented identity in flavor.', FALSE, '2025-02-23', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2959/picture?type=normal'),
(100111, 'Larios 12 Premium Gin Mediterránea', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Spain', 'Gin', 40, 'Larios 12 is an excellent quality Premium gin that is born from an exotic combination of 12 botanical species extracted directly from nature, in 5 distillations. It has the aromas of gin: wild juniper berries, coriander, nutmeg and Angelica root. Added to this are the most refreshing citrus fruits: Mediterranean lemon and orange, two types of mandarin - clementine mandarin and tangerine mandarin-, grapefruit and lime. And the distinctive touch, the orange blossom, to guarantee an exotic aroma, with a silky touch on the palate.', FALSE, '2025-01-13', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1395/picture?type=normal'),
(100207, 'Whitley Neill Quince Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 43, 'The Whitley and Neill families have been involved in the creation of fine spirits since 1762, using the very best ingredients from around the world. Their latest creation is the Whitley Neill Quince Gin. The aroma of fresh stone fruits appears immediately, gently followed by hints of juniper and citrus zest. The distinctive flavour of quince dominates the palate, giving way to the sweetness of apricots and peaches, with a long, fruity finish that opens out into orange blossoms and zesty grapefruit.', FALSE, '2025-02-26', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2971/picture?type=normal'),
(101312, 'Gabriel Boudier Saffron Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Gin', 40, 'Saffron Gin: the name alone is an invitation to go on a journey. The recipe goes back a long way: after being re-discovered in the Maison Boudier archives, it resulted in the revival of this unique gin. From London to Pondicherry, Saffron Gin is the aperitif for festive occasions, with a promise of the exotic.', FALSE, '2025-01-10', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1975/picture?type=normal'),
(100362, 'Broker''s Premium Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 40, 'Broker’s is a brand with personality and playfulness. Creators Martin and Andy Dawson chose the image of a bowler-hatted gentlemen – an archetypal stockbroker – to reflect the fact that historically England is the home of gin. Broker’s is a seriously good gin with a quirky marketing approach. Broker’s Gin is made in a 200-year-old distillery in the heart of England using a traditional copper pot-still. The recipe is as old as the distillery. A quadruple-distilled pure grain spirit made from English wheat is redistilled with ten traditional botanicals, creating a gin of outstanding flavour and smoothness. Broker’s Gin does not follow the modern trend of using weird and wonderful spirits and botanicals. There are no oddball ingredients in Broker’s Gin. We believe our forefathers did an unbeatable job perfecting gin recipes over many hundreds of years.', FALSE, '2025-02-21', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/533/picture?type=normal'),
(100279, 'Bombay Sapphire East', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 42, 'Originally created as a personal homage to the Far East, where our Master of Botanicals, Ivano Tonutti has spent much of his time sourcing exotic botanicals. Thai lemongrass and Vietnamese black peppercorns are added to our classic botanical blend. All 12 come together during vapor infusion to create a gin that truly stands apart. Infused by exotic eastern flavors, this wonderfully tasteful gin comes with more than added spice and a generous hint of citrus. Bottled at 42% ABV, it''s extra punchy too.', FALSE, '2025-02-26', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/462/picture?type=normal'),
(100107, 'Adamus Dry Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Portugal', 'Gin', 44.4, 'Unique and unmistakable, it is made from Bairrada berry from which you get a perfect distillate 44.4% Alc. A strong personality drink, capable of carry us to unique moments. It is in this context and the result of the research and development of Destilaria Levira, but also in its passion for distillation and combination of flavors and senses that is born Adamus Dry Gin.  The first year of Adamus Dry Gin production is 2015 and this is a limited serie of 4448 bottles.', FALSE, '2025-01-27', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2644/picture?type=normal'),
(100044, 'Mermaid Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 42, 'We use hand-picked ingredients such as Rock Samphire from a secret location on the sunny south side of the Island. All the hops we use are grown on the Island too! We want our spirits to be not only fresh, but to capture the true island spirit! Our Coriander seeds are the first to be commercially grown in England. Our Gin uses an infusion of carefully selected botanicals including Juniper Berries, rock samphire that is hand-picked from the Island’s chalk cliffs and Boadicea hops grown at the famous Ventnor Botanic Garden. Along with English coriander seeds, fresh lemon zest, angelica root, liquorish root, orris root, elderflower and grains of paradise. Before distilling commences, our botanicals are steeped together for 24 hours to enable all the essential oils in the botanicals to be released. Following this, the spirit is then distilled for a day. The fresh Mermaids Gin is rested for seven days to allow the flavours and aromas to mellow and marry together.', FALSE, '2025-02-22', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2434/picture?type=normal'),
(100413, 'Sharish Blue Magic', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Portugal', 'Gin', 40, 'António Cuco and his Gin Sharish not cease to amaze and now present Sharish - Blue Magic. Among the botanicals we can find strawberries, raspberries, cinnamon, cardamom, lemon, angelica root, ginger, licorice, coriander seeds and clear juniper. The star of this new Gin it''s a flower named Clitoria ternatea that gives the Gin a blue tone without the use of artificial coloring. According to the producer this Gin has a "magic touch" because when added to tonic water the mixture of liquids passes from blue to a light pink. This new release celebrates the first year of life of the Sharish project in the best way.', FALSE, '2025-01-15', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2020/picture?type=normal'),
(100574, 'Filliers Dry Gin 28', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Belgium', 'Gin', 46, 'Filliers Dry Gin 28 fully expresses the traditional craftmanship of Filliers, developed after decades of carefully distilling jenever. It was Firmin Filliers (°1888 - +1965), a member of the third generation of the Filliers master-distillers, who shortly after the end of the First World War in 1918, came up with the recipe for this handmade premium smooth gin. As is the case with jenever, juniper berries are the most important ingredient in gin. Enriched with 28 meticulousy selected botanicals, Filliers Dry Gin 28 delivers and exceptional and surprising taste experience!', FALSE, '2025-01-14', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/899/picture?type=normal'),
(100084, 'GINSTR Stuttgart Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Germany', 'Gin', 44, 'Ginstr Stuttgart Dry Gin is a love letter to Stuttgart. Here is everything Stuttgart: Only 711 bottles per filling, the Stuttgart airport code in the brand name and even the drums carry Stuttgarter name. So our first barrel is simply Killesberg! The ingredients come from Stuttgart and the surrounding region. Of the home-grown citrus fruits on juicy juniper berries from its own vineyards in Kernen. The previously thoroughly filtered and used for Ginstr Bodensee-water flavored with original Cannstatter mineral water. All botanicals that do not can be cultivated in Stuttgart, coming from regional dealers, for the most part from the Stuttgart Market Hall. Fresh citrus aromas, finest juniper, a hint of rosemary, cardamom and coriander for spiciness. Given licorice, kaffir lime leaves, orange blossom, hibiscus and pomegranate seeds for the perfect middle note. A total of 46 hand-picked botanicals find their way into Ginstr Stuttgart Dry Gin. Ginstr Stuttgart Dry Gin is self-produced and bottled. So the makers have constantly most control of the highest quality. And you can taste it.', FALSE, '2025-01-28', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/3290/picture?type=normal'),
(101370, 'Thomas Dakin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 42, 'Thomas Dakin Gin is a classic style London Dry Gin which takes its name from the forefather of English gin, Thomas Dakin, who created the world’s first quality gin in 1761 in the North West of England. Thomas Dakin Gin is distilled in small batches in a baby copper pot still. The Master Distiller uses a secret recipe of eleven botanicals, including some traditionally used for making cordials in the 18th Century, as well as juniper, orange peel and English coriander with the unique addition of red cole to give the gin its long, lingering finish. Horseradish, or red cole as it was known in Dakin’s day, was used to revive weary travellers journeying by coach and horses from London to Scotland.', FALSE, '2025-01-07', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2279/picture?type=normal'),
(100432, 'Sir Chill Gin - (Formerly Churchill''s Gin)', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Belgium', 'Gin', 37.5, 'Sir chill gin is an exceptional as well as an unique gin. Especially developed for the bon vivant who wants to explore. For Sir chill gin a selection was made of the best tobacco’s in the world, cultivated to a liquid extract. Besides this exceptional taste you will discover vanilla and tangerine aroma’s, which makes this aromatic gin a true experience for your palate. Perfect for the ladies combined with elderflower tonic water, as for the gentlemen with mediterranean tonic water. A gin that is accessible to everyone! The combination of aroma’s from all parts of the world all in one glass of Sir chill gin, will take you on a journey around the world like no other.', FALSE, '2025-01-08', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2865/picture?type=normal'),
(100176, 'Whitley Neill Raspberry Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 43, 'Raspberry Gin delivers an invigorating tartness from Scottish raspberries, complemented perfectly by undertones of liquorice and coriander, for a well-rounded finish.', FALSE, '2025-02-25', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/5242/picture?type=normal'),
(100347, 'Rock Rose Hand Crafted Scottish Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 41.5, 'Rock Rose gin gets its wonderful flavour from a carefully selected and put together creation of local and traditional botanicals. Each one meticulously chosen for their flavour properties to create the perfect taste.', FALSE, '2025-01-24', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1932/picture?type=normal'),
(100765, 'Generous Gin - Fresh & Aromatic', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Gin', 44, 'All the ingredients coming into the composition of Generous Gin are natural: Juniper, Citrus, Mandarin, Red Pepper, Jasmin & Elder Flower. Some of them are produced by maceration, others by distillation, using exclusively traditional methods. This naturality can be clearly perceived in the tasting: the style is clear, the flavours are precised and well harmonised. Fine and floral aroma. Dominant base of juniper, softened by the white flowers (elderflower, jasmine). A beautiful aromatic explosion of citrus fruits and spices highlighting the freshness of the juniper, with sweet floral notes and traces of jasmine. A good length in the mouth, enriched by the persistent notes of red pepper, citrus fruits and juniper.', FALSE, '2025-01-02', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/987/picture?type=normal'),
(100925, 'Audemus Pink Pepper Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Gin', 44, 'Pink Pepper Gin has been designed to be an entirely unique, intense and aromatic gin ­ one which will age and evolve both in the bottle and in the glass. When the bottle is young, or when diluted or chilled ­ fresher, spicy notes of pink pepper, juniper and cardamom are prominent. Over time, however, the liquid evolves and warms up ­ allowing notes of patisserie; vanilla, tonka and honey to come to the forefront. On the palate the gin is full­bodied and intensely aromatic, thus it is perfect for sipping or in cocktails.', FALSE, '2025-01-22', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/258/picture?type=normal'),
(100231, 'Williams Chase GB Great British Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 40, 'GB Gin is crafted by copper pot distilling Chase Potato Vodka with 10 botanicals; juniper (the buds and the berries), coriander seed, bitter almond, cinnamon bark, ginger, cloves, angelica root, liquorice root, lemon peel kibbles, and cardamon to create our GB extra dry gin. Zesty citrus nose and warm spicy notes. On the palate, juniper, lemon and rich spices. Full bodied with an extra dry finish.', FALSE, '2025-01-11', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2450/picture?type=normal'),
(100273, 'Puerto De Indias Strawberry Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Spain', 'Gin', 37.5, 'Premium Gin produced in one of the oldest distilleries of Andalusia, located in the town of Carmona in the province of Seville. With a translucent, light pink appearance, Port of India Strawberry Premium Gin has a soft touch of liquorice and a sweet, wild flavour of strawberry and juniper.', FALSE, '2025-01-14', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1878/picture?type=normal'),
(100255, 'Four Pillars Rare Dry Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Australia', 'Gin', 41.8, 'Four Pillars Rare Dry Gin is crafted to deliver the best of all worlds: a perfect, classic gin and also something that would fascinate and delight even the most hardened gin fanatic. It’s spicy but with great citrus, a truly modern Australian gin. Four Pillars Rare Dry Gin captures the essence of contemporary Australia’s heritage in Europe and Asia. We’re using whole oranges which is unusual but Australian citrus is highly aromatic and supports the spicier botanicals like cardamom. The cinnamon and star anise add rich fruitcake tones, the Tasmanian pepperberry leaf provides warmth rather than heat, and the lemon myrtle is a beautiful alternative to lemon peel.', FALSE, '2025-02-07', 'London Dry', 0, 'https://88bamboo.co/blogs/gin/taste-testing-the-og-four-pillars-rare-dry-gin-41-8', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/948/picture?type=normal'),
(100025, 'Z44 Distilled Dry Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Gin', 44, 'Look to the east from Tramin in South Tyrol and you can see the white flanks of the Weisshorn peak soaring up into the spring sunshine. These slopes are home to the pine cones that will in three years ripen to perfection, to be carefully picked by hand in the summer. These pine cones are what give our Z44 – Distilled Dry Gin its distinctive authenticity. Nuances of fresh lime and a range of Alpine and Mediterranean herbs and flowers from the foothills of the Alps complement the menthol-fresh pine taste to produce an innovative Distilled Dry Gin. The typical notes of juniper are complemented with yarrow, violet root and gentian root. The essence of pine cones is distilled in a small still, and the result is this unique Alpine gin.', FALSE, '2025-01-27', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2480/picture?type=normal'),
(100623, 'Edinburgh Seaside Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 43, 'Inspired by the East Coast shoreline near Edinburgh, Seaside Gin was the first of our collaborations with Heriot-Watt University’s Brewing & Distilling MSC.  Its shoreline botanicals including ground ivy, bladderwrack and scurvygrass contribute to a spirit with distinctive minerality. This is a finely balanced gin with a fresh sweetness on the nose, soft salinity and herbaceous notes on the palate, and a clean finish. Seaside Gin is at home in a crisp G&T, a briny Seaside Martini with olives and anchovy garnish and a variety of classic cocktails.', FALSE, '2025-02-28', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/838/picture?type=normal'),
(101217, 'Geranium', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 44, 'This Premium London Dry Gin was discovered by Hammer & Son. It took much practice to create the perfect gin, but with the discovery of the geranium plant, this London Dry Gin was created. Its classic, crisp, round taste is the reason why it has received the Gold Medal at the Wine & Spirits Tasting Competition of 2013.', FALSE, '2025-02-13', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/996/picture?type=normal'),
(101149, 'Brecon Botanicals Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 43, 'Made from our own unique recipe, combining a specially selected range of botanicals and the best pure grain spirit, this super-premium gin is produced in small batches using only the finest ingredients. The combination of botanicals, the best pure grain spirit and our own water from the Beacons makes this a truly exceptional gin and one which I''m sure the gin enthusiasts amongst us will appreciate.', FALSE, '2025-02-21', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/511/picture?type=normal'),
(101374, 'Four Pillars Navy Strength Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Australia', 'Gin', 58.8, 'After experimenting with some exclusive batches of a high-proof gin for the Gin Palace we decided to add fresh ''Judy''s Everbearing’ native finger limes, alongside our beautiful organic oranges, for its first release in 2014. This fresh citrus goes into the botanical basket, with some fresh ginger, giving our Navy Strength Gin its signature power and intensity. The finger limes highlight the Asian spices like coriander and star anise, and are complemented by the fresh ginger. Then the turmeric adds a fresh but earthy quality, not unlike dill, and weight to the palate. The resulting gin has lifted aromatics of lime curd, pine needles, and fragrant spices with a vanilla character which pulls the spices together. The palate is intense - sweet and juicy - but it is still very clean.', FALSE, '2025-02-28', 'Navy Strength', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/947/picture?type=normal'),
(100043, 'Bombay Sapphire Sunset - Limited Edition', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 43, 'Infused with warming spices and bittersweet Spanish mandarin, Bombay Sapphire Sunset is the perfect gin for reconnecting and unwinding with friends, as the sun descends and day becomes night. A unique aromatic flavour expression of Bombay Sapphire, combining the ten signature exotic Bombay Sapphire botanicals with an additional three – golden turmeric, Indian white cardamom, and Spanish mandarin to create a complex but beautifully balanced, vibrant gin. Bombay Sapphire Sunset is the perfect sundowner, best enjoyed in a Sunset & Tonic accompanied by an orange wheel and star anise. The unique addition of an orange wheel is a simple yet striking garnish to enhance the botanical flavours of this unique special edition.', FALSE, '2025-01-01', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/7674/picture?type=normal'),
(100936, 'Cannabis Sativa Gin - Fibre Hemp Flavoured', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Netherlands', 'Gin', 40, 'Cannabis Sativa Gin, is a Dutch-produced gin by Dutch Windmill Spirts. This Gin is infused with cannabis which you will certainly taste in the taste. This cannabis gin does not contain THC.', FALSE, '2025-01-01', 'Flavoured Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/5127/picture?type=normal'),
(100769, 'Nouaison Gin - By G''Vine', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Gin', 45, 'Maison Villevert has changed the recipe and updated the packaging for its G''Vine Nouaison gin brand. Nouaison by G’Vine is crafted in France from grapes, combined with 14 botanicals that are carefully selected. Crafted by Master Distiller and creator of G''Vine gin de France, Jean-Sébastien Robicquet, Nouaison, meaning ‘setting’, represents the metamorphosis stage of the star ingredient, the grape, from aromatic vine flower to luscious grape berry. Framed by the grape smoothness, rich and intense, Nouaison Gin by G’Vine explores a large flavour palette evoking hitherto unseen aromas such as sandalwood, bergamot, prune and vetiveria. The revamped gin, which first appeared in 2008, sees the addition of four botanicals and the abv move up from 43.9% to 45%.', FALSE, '2025-02-04', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/5329/picture?type=normal'),
(101524, 'Arctic Blue Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Finland', 'Gin', 10, 'This is the moment. The precious fleeting moment of fresh morning dew in the pristine forests of Finland. The shortest of whiles when the delicate scents of moist arctic blueberry shrubs and spruce needles embrace in perfect harmony. We wanted to capture this moment. To confine it in a bottle for you to taste and savour. All genuine and most delicate aromas of arctic blueberries, or bilberries as they are called, are preserved in our gin. This is why it turns into an elegant misty white shade when mixed with tonic water. All the ingredients are carefully selected and distilled in small batches to ensure the premium quality of Arctic Blue Gin. The bilberries used in our artisan gin grow wild in the forest near Koli National Park and other close-by areas in the Karelia region. This is where bilberries have an exceptionally succulent taste and high level of nutrients. Arctic Blue Gin is distilled with pride in Ilomantsi, Finland.', FALSE, '2025-02-13', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/5456/picture?type=normal'),
(100592, 'Barr Hill Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Gin', 45, 'The gin is a celebration of our special connection to the land. We use pure grain spirits as a canvas to showcase juniper berry and raw northern honey. Added just before bottling, the raw honey imparts unique floral qualities that vary with season and blossom. Our distillery, on the banks of the Lamoille River in the Northeast Kingdom, is rooted in the agriculture of Vermont. Hardwick, Caledonia Country, is a community inspired by farms where the production of milk, cheese, timber, grains, honey, seeds, and herbs are part of our lives and help define our place.', FALSE, '2025-01-30', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/292/picture?type=normal'),
(100676, 'Clouds Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Switzerland', 'Gin', 42, 'Do not ever put the Clouds in the clouds. If the weather is clear, the guests see in the restaurant and bistro in the highest building in Switzerland via Zurich city to the mountains. Or from the bar-side up in the Aargau. And that there is a bar manager Andreas Kloke traveled to create with us the Clouds Gin. Fresh aromas of oranges, tangerines and some juniper in the nose, spicy aromas of thyme and sage, resin and cardamom on the palate. So to be a trendy gin!', FALSE, '2025-02-08', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/639/picture?type=normal'),
(101440, 'Gin De Cologne', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Germany', 'Gin', 42, 'Our gin de cologne is hand-crafted in Cologne-Ehrenfeld. With over 12 botanicals such as peel of lemons, oranges and limes, lavender and hibiscus flowers and of course juniper. From the idea to produce a gin with passion and devotion, which convinces not only by its taste, but also spreads the feeling of the Cologne spirit, the high-quality and delicious Gin de Cologne arose.', FALSE, '2025-02-15', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/5332/picture?type=normal'),
(100988, 'Bleu D''Argent London Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Gin', 40, 'This is a French made gin in a typical London Dry guise using 9 botanicals in its final distillation. The distillery is located in the north of France in the Petersbach commune. Better known as the Alsace wine region. Juniper led, but with very obvious coriander, citrus and pepper spice.', FALSE, '2025-02-13', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/429/picture?type=normal'),
(100995, 'Tranquebar Colonial Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Netherlands', 'Gin', 45, 'The taste is Tranquebar Gin a classic Colonial Gin, with a warm full-bodied, soft spicy flavor of juniper, cardamom and cinnamon with a fresh breath of Orange and Citrus. The recipe also remains the same, and consists besides the classic Gin herbs Juniper, Coriander, Orange peel, Lemon peel and Angelikarod also of the more exotic such as cardamom, cinnamon and nutmeg Darjeeling tea, all from the East Indies. Our "Master Distiller" Michael Schultz, distill and bottle Tranquebar Gin in small batches, with individual bottle number and vintage indication.', FALSE, '2025-02-23', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2301/picture?type=normal'),
(101316, 'Tarquin''s Gin - The Seadog Navy Strength ', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 57, 'Southwestern Distillery''s excellent Tarquin''s Gin bottled at 57% abv! Orris root, green cardamom seeds, cinnamon and violets are all used and the gin is distilled in Tamara, their copper pot still named after the goddess of the Tamar.', FALSE, '2025-01-31', 'Navy Strength', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2225/picture?type=normal'),
(100269, 'Gillemore', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Belgium', 'Gin', 46, 'It all began in the ancient city of Bruges. It seemed like an ordinary day for 19-year-old Louis Gillemon, but little did he know … he was already smitten with the chemistry of gin distillation. Since gin is a spirit, which derives its flavours from different herbs, he was on the lookout for the magical combination that was so sweet it would conquer the heart of female epicureans. Master chefs, who were looking over his shoulder during the distillation in the copper still, were dazzled but he kept saying: ''I can do better than that'' … and he did. Sharing Gillemore gin with friends and lovers, creates magical moments …', FALSE, '2025-01-03', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1008/picture?type=normal'),
(101111, 'Ginscape London Dry Gin', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Denmark', 'Gin', 43.7, 'Ginscape is a Danish London Dry Gin distilled with organic sea buckthorn berries from the Danish island Bornholm. A perfect and elegant impression. Elegant nose with soft notes of sea buckthorn and distinctive tints of crispy juniper. Smooth and soft base with stunning balance between juniper, coriander, citrus and orange, and a smooth finish with notes of sea buckthorn that vanishes into liquorice. GinScape is a new and modern passionate Danish gin bringning your gin & tonic as well as your cocktail to a new and higher level.', FALSE, '2025-02-13', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/4338/picture?type=normal'),
(101277, 'Twisted Nose Watercress Dry Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 40, 'Distilled at the Winchester Distillery, our small batch gin combines ten botanicals including local watercress to create a spirit that is intense, fragrant and refreshing. The Romans knew watercress as Nasturtium, meaning “twisted nose”, from which our gin takes its name. On drinking, pine notes of Juniper emerge first followed by fresh citrus and deeper spice tones. A sparkle of peppery watercress appears next as the spicy oils build on the tongue, awakening your senses to the more subtle flavours of the remaining botanicals. The finish is long and satisfying with fresh citrus lingering until the following mouthful.', FALSE, '2025-02-16', 'London Dry', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/2316/picture?type=normal'),
(100678, 'Kintyre Botanical Gin', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 43, 'Beinn an Tuirc Distillery proudly presents Kintyre Gin, a beautifully blended spirit using carefully selected botanicals which reflect our unique coastal, pasture and woodland position on the east coast of the Kintyre peninsula. We use 12 botanicals in our core expression, Kintyre Gin, which have all been sustainably sourced. To achieve the characteristics of a very flavoursome and well-balanced spirit, the gin consists of 10 commonly used botanicals, with the addition of 2 which are unique, namely Icelandic moss and sheep sorrel - both grow on the estate in abundance. Either through maceration or vapour infusion, these produce a gin which our expert tasting panel described as having earthy and spicy characteristics, being deep in flavour, with a very pleasant floral aroma. A true taste of Kintyre. Kintyre Gin is sustainably produced using our very own renewable energy, powered from the small hydro-electric scheme at Torrisdale Castle Estate. Our water is sourced from the hill from which we take our name. ‘Beinn an Tuirc’ translates from gaelic as ‘The Hill of the Wild Boar’ and is the highest point in Kintyre, located above our distillery building.', FALSE, '2025-01-02', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/3512/picture?type=normal'),
(100840, 'Isfjord Arctic Gin - (Also known as 69°N Gin)', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Greenland', 'Gin', 44, 'Distilled with 12 of the finest botanicals. Carefully well balanced with a full scent of juniper berries, making way for lemon grass and the soft tones of angelica root, a little touch of cardemom, ending with a slighty sweet and bitter tone of orange. Not to mention the remarkable smoothness from distilling with the iceberg water of Greenland. Ladies and Gentlemen – this is not a Dry Gin! Isfjord Premium Arctic Gin is probably the smoothest Gin you can ever find. It´s the perfect alternative for newcomers to the Gin world, for the experienced, the experts, and all Gin lovers…and the haters as well.', FALSE, '2025-02-27', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1283/picture?type=normal'),
(101209, 'Batch Signature Gin', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United Kingdom', 'Gin', 40, 'Our unique recipe for Batch gin has been developed with a tiny 25 litre column still. To make this exquisite gin, we first produce a pure vodka with a minimum of five distillations. Then in a final distillation the smooth and creamy vodka passes through the ‘gin head’ filled with juniper berries, coriander seeds, cinnamon bark and angelica root - creating the core body of gin; then, inspired by ancient Moor and Turk spice markets, we add fresh lemongrass stalks, orange peel, cardamoms, cloves, crushed nutmegs, allspice berries and our signature frankincense and myrrh blend, for a sublimely rich gin.', FALSE, '2025-02-25', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/298/picture?type=normal'),
(100115, 'Inverroche Gin Classic', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'South Africa', 'Gin', 43, 'Inveroche Gin Classic is a modern hand-crafted spirit infused with 15 botanicals and double distilled to extract the pure and subtle flavours. It is a richly textured, crisp Gin which blends traditional and hand harvested African botanicals. Soft juniper top notes are followed by fresh citrus aromas. Angelica root and cassia bark give depth and a lingering organic feel while the coriander seed and cardamom pods impart delicate warmth. The subtle perfumed undertones of the cape fynbos flora amplify the aromas of the classic botanicals and enhance complexity. Drink it in a cognac snifter on lots of ice or in a large balloon wine glass with tonic and a curl of lemon zest.', FALSE, '2025-02-17', 'Distilled Gin', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ginventory.reed.be/api/v2/products/1274/picture?type=normal'),
