(101145, 'Fernet-Branca', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 39, 'Fernet-Branca was created in 1845 by Bernardino Branca in Milan where it is still made today. It is made from a proprietary recipe of 27 different herbs, roots, and spices only some of which are disclosed. They include: aloe ferox, bitter orange, chamomile, cardamom, cinchona bark, cinnamon, galangal, gentian, iris, laurel, laraha, linden, myrrh, zedoary and saffron. It is aged in 15,000-20,000 liter Slovenian oak vats for at least a year. Due to the popularity of the brand in Argentina, a second distillery located outside of Buenos Aires was founded in 1941. Fernet-Branca & Coke is how it is most consumed there. Fernet-Branca was created in 1845 by Bernardino Branca in Milan where it is still made today. It is made from a proprietary recipe of 27 different herbs, roots, and spices only some of which are disclosed. They include: aloe ferox, bitter orange, chamomile, cardamom, cinchona bark, cinnamon, galangal, gentian, iris, laurel, laraha, linden, myrrh, zedoary and saffron.  It is aged in 15,000-20,000 liter Slovenian oak vats for at least a year. Due to the popularity of the brand in Argentina, a second distillery located outside of Buenos Aires was founded in 1941. Fernet-Branca & Coke is how it is most consumed there.', FALSE, '2025-01-22', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/000ce4f0-d419-0136-de35-12541730c456/fernet_branca_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100380, 'Mr Black Single Origin Colombia', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Australia', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 25, 'Mr Black Single Origin Colombia is the first in a new limited edition series which will highlight a different coffee region in each release. The Colombia Single Origin expression is made from 100% Caturra arabica grown in Finca Villa Betulia near Hulia, Colombia. Luis Aníbal Calderón and his family grew the coffee and together they have over 60 years experience growing coffee and 12 years focusing on specialty coffee. Only 6000 bottles are available globally with just 600 headed to the States. Mr Black Single Origin Colombia is the first in a new limited edition series which will highlight a different coffee region in each release. The Colombia Single Origin expression is made from 100% Caturra arabica grown in Finca Villa Betulia near Hulia, Colombia. Luis Aníbal Calderón and his family grew the coffee and together they have over 60 years experience growing coffee and 12 years focusing on specialty coffee. Only 6000 bottles are available globally with just 600 headed to the States.', FALSE, '2025-01-12', 'Coffee', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/5ce80970-f2dd-0137-fca0-5235e97b0d32/mr_black_single_origin_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100487, 'Ferrand Dry Curaçao Yuzu Late Harvest', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Like the Ferrand Dry Curaçao released in 2012, Maison Ferrand owner Alexandre Gabriel made this Yuzu Late Harvest Dry Curaçao in consultation with drinks historian David Wondrich. The yuzu fruit which was sourced from L''Agrumiste, a biodiverse orchard in the Mediterranean, was allowed to be harvested past its peak maturity in February rather than the fall. The whole yuzu fruit is macerated in grape spirit for a week and then distilled. Then the yuzu distillate is married with a touch of yuzu infusion, bourbon vanilla, brandy, and Ferrand Cognac. Availability for the US begins July 2023 nationwide. (SRP $35. Like the Ferrand Dry Curaçao released in 2012, Maison Ferrand owner Alexandre Gabriel made this Yuzu Late Harvest Dry Curaçao in consultation with drinks historian David Wondrich. The yuzu fruit which was sourced from L''Agrumiste, a biodiverse orchard in the Mediterranean, was allowed to be harvested past its peak maturity in February rather than the fall. The whole yuzu fruit is macerated in grape spirit for a week and then distilled. Then the yuzu distillate is married with a touch of yuzu infusion, bourbon vanilla, brandy, and Ferrand Cognac. Availability for the US begins July 2023 nationwide. (SRP $35.99)', FALSE, '2025-02-23', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/c12864f0-eddb-013b-a2c9-6afb4d8fac64/fernand-yuzu-dry-curacao_original-1691103456.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100610, 'Drambuie', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Scotland', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'An essential ingredient in a handful of classic cocktail, including the Rusty Nail, Drambuie -- a Scotch whisky liqueur -- is flavored with spices, herbs and heather honey. The company dates its origins to the mid-1700s, when it was supposedly created for Bonnie Prince Charlie by his Royal Apothecary. In 2014, William Grant & Sons acquired the brand, which is still blended in Glasgow, Scotland. Its name is derived from the Scots Gaelic term ‘An Dram Buidheach,’ meaning “The Drink that Satisfies. An essential ingredient in a handful of classic cocktail, including the Rusty Nail, Drambuie -- a Scotch whisky liqueur -- is flavored with spices, herbs and heather honey. The company dates its origins to the mid-1700s, when it was supposedly created for Bonnie Prince Charlie by his Royal Apothecary. In 2014, William Grant & Sons acquired the brand, which is still blended in Glasgow, Scotland. Its name is derived from the Scots Gaelic term ‘An Dram Buidheach,’ meaning “The Drink that Satisfies.”', FALSE, '2025-02-15', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/0a4e8cb0-e09d-0136-cda0-7690e26e02a2/drambuie_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101504, 'Lo-Fi Aperitifs Gentian Amaro', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 16, 'Lo-Fi Aperitifs is a collaboration between Ernest & Julio Gallo Winery and Steven Grasse of Quaker City Mercantile, combining expertise in wine, spirits, and brand creation. The tandem then sought bartender input in the creation of their products, including from brand ambassador Claire Sprouse. Its Gentian Amaro is made with a base of white wine fortified with grape spirits. Botanicals include anise, cinchona bark, orange oil bitters, hibiscus, grapefruit, ginger, bois de rose (rosewood), and gentian root. Lo-Fi Aperitifs is a collaboration between Ernest & Julio Gallo Winery and Steven Grasse of Quaker City Mercantile, combining expertise in wine, spirits, and brand creation. The tandem then sought bartender input in the creation of their products, including from brand ambassador Claire Sprouse. Its Gentian Amaro is made with a base of white wine fortified with grape spirits. Botanicals include anise, cinchona bark, orange oil bitters, hibiscus, grapefruit, ginger, bois de rose (rosewood), and gentian root.', FALSE, '2025-02-10', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/82fbd7c0-8d9b-0137-515c-1227e42105cd/lofi_gentian_amaro_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101169, 'St. Germain Elderflower Liqueur', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 20, 'St. Germain took the cocktail world by storm when it debuted as the first available elderflower liqueur in 2007. To make the liqueur, elderflower petals are macerated in grape eau-de-vie, with the resulting combination then sweetened. St. Germain was created by the late Robert Cooper, and is now a part of the Bacardi portfolio. . St. Germain took the cocktail world by storm when it debuted as the first available elderflower liqueur in 2007. To make the liqueur, elderflower petals are macerated in grape eau-de-vie, with the resulting combination then sweetened. St. Germain was created by the late Robert Cooper, and is now a part of the Bacardi portfolio.', FALSE, '2025-01-19', 'Floral', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/c91352b0-cc46-0136-8042-72da7977098e/st_germain_elderflower_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100046, 'Mozart Chocolate Cream Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Austria', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 17, 'Mozart Chocolate Cream is a milk chocolate liqueur made with cocoa from West Africa, Madagascar Bourbon vanilla, and Belgian chocolate. The distillate is made with sugar beets which is also the source of its sugar to sweeten the liqueur. The distillery is located in Salzburg, Austria -- the birthplace of Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart. . Mozart Chocolate Cream is a milk chocolate liqueur made with cocoa from West Africa, Madagascar Bourbon vanilla, and Belgian chocolate. The distillate is made with sugar beets which is also the source of its sugar to sweeten the liqueur. The distillery is located in Salzburg, Austria -- the birthplace of Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart.', FALSE, '2025-02-27', 'Chocolate', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/1ce512f0-ec99-0136-2b21-32f1c51e1058/mozart_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101215, 'Pierre Ferrand Dry Curaçao', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Pierre Ferrand Dry Curaçao is based on a 19th century recipe and made in consultation with cocktail historian David Wondrich. It''s made by infusing bitter laraha orange peels for one week in grape spirit. Then this infusion is distilled. Separately, walnut skins and prunes are infused for several months in brandy and Pierre Ferrand cognac to create a vegetal infusion. Then the master blender blends the orange distillate, the vegetal infusion, along with brandy and Pierre Ferrand cognac. Toasted cane sugar, which is barrel aged for several months, is used to sweeten the blend. Pierre Ferrand Dry Curaçao is based on a 19th century recipe and made in consultation with cocktail historian David Wondrich. It''s made by infusing bitter laraha orange peels for one week in grape spirit. Then this infusion is distilled. Separately, walnut skins and prunes are infused for several months in brandy and Pierre Ferrand cognac to create a vegetal infusion. Then the master blender blends the orange distillate, the vegetal infusion, along with brandy and Pierre Ferrand cognac. Toasted cane sugar, which is barrel aged for several months, is used to sweeten the blend. Finally, the Dry Curaçao is left to age for several months in French oak barrels before bottling.', FALSE, '2025-01-09', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/ff985070-b62b-0136-4f61-3677833961d5/pierre_ferrand_dry_curacao_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101470, 'Mr Black Cold Brew Coffee Liqueur', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Australia', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 25, 'Mr Black Cold Brew Coffee Liqueur is made at a coffee roastery and distillery located just outside of Sydney, Australia. It uses a base spirit of Australian wheat vodka along with cold-brewed coffee made from 100% Arabica coffee beans. No caramel, vanilla, or artificial flavors added. . Mr Black Cold Brew Coffee Liqueur is made at a coffee roastery and distillery located just outside of Sydney, Australia. It uses a base spirit of Australian wheat vodka along with cold-brewed coffee made from 100% Arabica coffee beans. No caramel, vanilla, or artificial flavors added.', FALSE, '2025-01-17', 'Coffee', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/31329b30-e9ca-0136-3c55-62a8e2797a14/mr_black_cold_brew_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101053, 'Mozart Chocolate Coffee Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Austria', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 17, 'Mozart Distillerie produces chocolate liqueurs in Salzburg, Austria — birthplace of composer Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart. This Chocolate Coffee expression is a permanent part of the portfolio and is made with West African cocoa, Belgian chocolate, Arabica coffee, Madagascar vanilla and cream from the Netherlands. It''s gluten free and bottled at 17% ABV. (SRP $29. Mozart Distillerie produces chocolate liqueurs in Salzburg, Austria — birthplace of composer Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart. This Chocolate Coffee expression is a permanent part of the portfolio and is made with West African cocoa, Belgian chocolate, Arabica coffee, Madagascar vanilla and cream from the Netherlands. It''s gluten free and bottled at 17% ABV. (SRP $29.99 per 750ml)', FALSE, '2025-01-09', 'Chocolate', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/5accde40-4fa7-013a-5d21-6a0ec6afd13c/mozard_chocolate_coffee_original-1688675839.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101287, 'Luxardo Cherry "Sangue Morlacco" Liqueur', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 30, 'Part of the Luxardo portfolio since 1821, Luxardo Cherry "Sangue Morlacco" is flavored with marasca cherry, a variety of sour cherries. Sangue Morlacco translates to “Morlacco blood,” referring to the liqueur’s deep red color and a group of people from the Dalmatian hinterland from the 17th and 18th centuries. Part of the Luxardo portfolio since 1821, Luxardo Cherry "Sangue Morlacco" is flavored with marasca cherry, a variety of sour cherries. Sangue Morlacco translates to “Morlacco blood,” referring to the liqueur’s deep red color and a group of people from the Dalmatian hinterland from the 17th and 18th centuries. The name was coined by Italian poet Gabriele D’Annunzio in 1919, after which the liqueur was renamed nearly a century after its creation.', FALSE, '2025-02-01', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/28010a70-ce6a-0136-ea04-4e63380ab660/luxardo_cherry_sangue_morlacco_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100866, 'Ancho Reyes Ancho Chile Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Mexico', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'This Ancho chile liqueur was inspired by the menjurjes, or homemade liqueurs, shared by artists and intellectuals who spent their evenings drinking together in Puebla cantinas throughout the 1920s. The recipe is based on an old family recipe and is made from ancho chiles grown on local farms in Puebla, Mexico. Poblano chiles are picked after they have ripened to a red color (effectively making them ancho chiles) and are then dried in the sun for up to 20 days. These are then sliced into smaller pieces and infused in neutral cane spirit from Veracruz, Mexico, for six months. This Ancho chile liqueur was inspired by the menjurjes, or homemade liqueurs, shared by artists and intellectuals who spent their evenings drinking together in Puebla cantinas throughout the 1920s. The recipe is based on an old family recipe and is made from ancho chiles grown on local farms in Puebla, Mexico. Poblano chiles are picked after they have ripened to a red color (effectively making them ancho chiles) and are then dried in the sun for up to 20 days. These are then sliced into smaller pieces and infused in neutral cane spirit from Veracruz, Mexico, for six months. The resulting liqueur is bottled at 40% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-02-17', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/09f59e50-b94e-0136-e901-7a6465a1878b/ancho_reyes_ancho_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100087, 'Cappelletti Mazzura Aperitivo', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 17, 'This aperitivo expression is a vegan offshoot of the brand''s signature Trivento style. It is made in the northern region of Trentino-Alto Adige in with a blend of flowers and fruits from the Dolomite hills and valleys with no artificial coloring or flavors. It is bottled at 17% ABV. . This aperitivo expression is a vegan offshoot of the brand''s signature Trivento style. It is made in the northern region of Trentino-Alto Adige in with a blend of flowers and fruits from the Dolomite hills and valleys with no artificial coloring or flavors. It is bottled at 17% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-01-18', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/de6e1ff0-f42d-013b-2ca3-72239e3d5d5d/cappelletti-mazzura-aperitivo_original-1687811615.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101270, 'Grand Marnier Cuvée du Centenaire', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Grand Marnier Cuvée du Centenaire was first introduced in 1927 to commemorate the 100th anniversary of the House of Marnier Lapostolle. Like the flagship Grand Marnier bottling, this is a blend of cognac and bitter orange distillate. However for this bottle, only XO cognacs from Grande and Petite Champagne crus are used. . Grand Marnier Cuvée du Centenaire was first introduced in 1927 to commemorate the 100th anniversary of the House of Marnier Lapostolle. Like the flagship Grand Marnier bottling, this is a blend of cognac and bitter orange distillate. However for this bottle, only XO cognacs from Grande and Petite Champagne crus are used.', FALSE, '2025-02-10', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/bdd8b070-afe6-0136-bcc9-1eaec77374f8/grand_marnier_cuvee_du_centenaire_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101030, 'Chartreuse Green Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 55, 'Green Chartreuse was first made in 1737 by Carthusian monks using a recipe for an elixir they were given in 1605. It is made from 130 plants and herbs which are crushed, macerated, and distilled in a manner which is today known in its entirety by two monks in France. Its green color is naturally derived. Bottled at 55% ABV, this is stronger and spicier than the Yellow version. Green Chartreuse was first made in 1737 by Carthusian monks using a recipe for an elixir they were given in 1605. It is made from 130 plants and herbs which are crushed, macerated, and distilled in a manner which is today known in its entirety by two monks in France. Its green color is naturally derived. Bottled at 55% ABV, this is stronger and spicier than the Yellow version. An essential ingredient in a Last Word cocktail.', FALSE, '2025-01-31', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/d99243d0-e566-0136-9212-2657365a3cd8/green_chartreuse_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101494, 'Fernet Leopold Highland Amaro', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Introduced in 2012, Fernet Leopold Highland Amaro is made in Colorado with over 20 botanicals including three types of mint, rose petals, elderflower, chamomile, and honeysuckle. Other disclosed botanicals include gentian root, lavender, ginger, sarsaparilla, and cocoa nibs. Introduced in 2012, Fernet Leopold Highland Amaro is made in Colorado with over 20 botanicals including three types of mint, rose petals, elderflower, chamomile, and honeysuckle. Other disclosed botanicals include gentian root, lavender, ginger, sarsaparilla, and cocoa nibs. It is aged in former Napa Valley chardonnay wine casks and bottled at 80 proof.', FALSE, '2025-02-03', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/3ebc1240-d41b-0136-65b3-7e2383dffb93/fernet_lepold_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100913, 'John D. Taylor''s Velvet Falernum', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Barbados', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 11, 'Velvet Falernum is a liqueur flavored with lime, almond, and spices. Today, John D Taylor''s version — which some refer to as the original falernum — is produced by R.L. Seale Ltd. in Barbados. The rum-based liqueur is bottled at 11% ABV and can be used in a variety of drinks such as swizzles, daiquiris, and Mai Tais among others. Velvet Falernum is a liqueur flavored with lime, almond, and spices. Today, John D Taylor''s version — which some refer to as the original falernum — is produced by R.L. Seale Ltd. in Barbados. The rum-based liqueur is bottled at 11% ABV and can be used in a variety of drinks such as swizzles, daiquiris, and Mai Tais among others.', FALSE, '2025-02-01', 'Other', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/b3bdd850-f1b4-0136-a5c6-76ae2bc8fcf6/velvet_falernum_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100203, 'Mozart Dark Chocolate Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Austria', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 17, 'Mozart Distillerie produces chocolate liqueurs in Salzburg, Austria — birthplace of composer Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart. This Dark Chocolate expression is a permanent part of the portfolio and is made with cocoa from West Africa and vanilla from Madagascar. It''s gluten-free and unlike the other expression in the portfolio, it''s also lactose-free and vegan. It''s bottled at 17% ABV. (SRP $29.99 per 750ml) . Mozart Distillerie produces chocolate liqueurs in Salzburg, Austria — birthplace of composer Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart. This Dark Chocolate expression is a permanent part of the portfolio and is made with cocoa from West Africa and vanilla from Madagascar. It''s gluten-free and unlike the other expression in the portfolio, it''s also lactose-free and vegan. It''s bottled at 17% ABV. (SRP $29.99 per 750ml)', FALSE, '2025-02-08', 'Chocolate', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/b9a34960-85c5-0139-182e-1e582fac410f/mozard_chocolate_dark_original-1688675850.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100958, 'Bénédictine', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Bénédictine was first made by Benedictine monks in Normandy in 1510. The recipe was rediscovered in 1863, by a wine merchant named Alexandre Le Grand who discovered it in a book and relaunched the ubiquitous liqueur. Made with 27 herbs and spices, Bénédictine is essential for making mainstays like the Vieux Carré and the B&B. (Bénédictine & Brandy). Bénédictine was first made by Benedictine monks in Normandy in 1510. The recipe was rediscovered in 1863, by a wine merchant named Alexandre Le Grand who discovered it in a book and relaunched the ubiquitous liqueur. Made with 27 herbs and spices, Bénédictine is essential for making mainstays like the Vieux Carré and the B&B. (Bénédictine & Brandy)', FALSE, '2025-01-12', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/b7c48b00-e536-0136-990f-221c5f9f19ba/dom_benedictine_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100052, 'Zirbenz Stone Pine Liqueur of the Alps', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Austria', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 35, 'Zirbenz is owned by Haus Alpenz and is made and bottled by Josef Hofer in Austria, a distillery that’s been in operation since 1797. The distinctive liqueur is made from the fruit of the Arolla Stone Pine tree. It is released each year in limited quantities, and may vary in taste from season to season. . Zirbenz is owned by Haus Alpenz and is made and bottled by Josef Hofer in Austria, a distillery that’s been in operation since 1797. The distinctive liqueur is made from the fruit of the Arolla Stone Pine tree. It is released each year in limited quantities, and may vary in taste from season to season.', FALSE, '2025-02-01', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/d0f76db0-ce77-0136-ea0a-4e63380ab660/zirbenz_stone_pine_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100060, 'Aperol', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 11, 'Aperol first debuted a century ago, in 1919. Known for its orange hue, and today for the ubiquitous and eponymous Aperol Spritz, Aperol is flavored with ingredients including cinchona, rhubarb, and gentian. Aperol first debuted a century ago, in 1919. Known for its orange hue, and today for the ubiquitous and eponymous Aperol Spritz, Aperol is flavored with ingredients including cinchona, rhubarb, and gentian. The bittersweet liqueur has been a part of the Campari portfolio since 2003.', FALSE, '2025-02-02', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/973f69f0-cc46-0136-5662-020e31d48091/aperol_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101457, 'Averna Amaro', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 29, 'Averna Amaro was first made in Sicily by the Averna family in 1868, after the recipe was gifted to them by Benedictine monk Frà Girolamo. Since then, descendants of the brand’s founder Salvatore Averna have passed the recipe down through the generations and grown the brand to international fame. Averna Amaro was first made in Sicily by the Averna family in 1868, after the recipe was gifted to them by Benedictine monk Frà Girolamo. Since then, descendants of the brand’s founder Salvatore Averna have passed the recipe down through the generations and grown the brand to international fame. The amaro is made with herbs and spices common throughout the Mediterranean and bottled at 29% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-02-24', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/ee005500-b9fe-0136-7f32-1ef466691924/averna_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100079, 'Luxardo Maraschino Liqueur', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 32, 'Luxardo Maraschino Liqueur is a clear cherry liqueur made from Sour Marasca cherries which are cultivated exclusively by the Luxardo family in the orchards of the Euganean Hills in Veneto. The cherries including the stones, branches and leaves are placed in larchwood vats for two years to infuse with neutral alcohol. Then the infusion including the solids is distilled and the heart of the cherry distillate is aged in large Finnish ash wood vats for a 12-18 months. Water and sugar is added prior to bottling at 64 proof. Luxardo Maraschino Liqueur is a clear cherry liqueur made from Sour Marasca cherries which are cultivated exclusively by the Luxardo family in the orchards of the Euganean Hills in Veneto. The cherries including the stones, branches and leaves are placed in larchwood vats for two years to infuse with neutral alcohol. Then the infusion including the solids is distilled and the heart of the cherry distillate is aged in large Finnish ash wood vats for a 12-18 months. Water and sugar is added prior to bottling at 64 proof.', FALSE, '2025-01-28', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/c7c05cc0-b9f9-0136-665f-0a26fc436cd2/luxardo_maraschino_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101351, 'Ancho Reyes Verde Chile Poblano Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Mexico', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Ancho Reyes Verde Chile Poblano Liqueur is made in a similar manner to the Ancho Reyes’ original ancho chile liqueur, with a few key differences: Instead of allowing the poblano peppers to ripen and sun dry, the poblano peppers for Ancho Reyes Verde are picked while they are still green. Some of those peppers are then fire roasted and all of the peppers are mashed before the maceration process begins. Ancho Reyes Verde Chile Poblano Liqueur is made in a similar manner to the Ancho Reyes’ original ancho chile liqueur, with a few key differences: Instead of allowing the poblano peppers to ripen and sun dry, the poblano peppers for Ancho Reyes Verde are picked while they are still green. Some of those peppers are then fire roasted and all of the peppers are mashed before the maceration process begins. It is then blended for consistency and bottled at 40% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-01-30', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/32623fe0-b951-0136-b4f7-76deb9107338/ancho_reyes_verde_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100249, 'Cocalero Negro', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Multiple Countries', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 29, 'Cocalero Negro is a product from Intrepid Spirits, based in Dublin, Ireland, that is inspired by South American ingredients from the Andes region. Building on the original botanical liqueur, Cocalero, this expression adds Aji Panca—which turns from red to black when dried in the sun, hence the name—and Locoto peppers. It is bottled at 29% ABV and available as of May, 2021. Note: price is based on 700 mL bottle. Cocalero Negro is a product from Intrepid Spirits, based in Dublin, Ireland, that is inspired by South American ingredients from the Andes region. Building on the original botanical liqueur, Cocalero, this expression adds Aji Panca—which turns from red to black when dried in the sun, hence the name—and Locoto peppers. It is bottled at 29% ABV and available as of May, 2021. Note: price is based on 700 mL bottle.', FALSE, '2025-02-26', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/6f82d360-c632-0139-adbf-16b4e60998e7/cocalero_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100368, 'Apologue Celery Root Herbal Liqueur', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 37, 'Apologue Celery Root Herbal Liqueur is made by a Chicago-based company which features regional ingredients from independent farmers. In addition to celery root, ingredients include anise seed, celery stalk, cinchona bark, dill, fennel seed, lemon peel, summer savory, and tarragon. It is sweetened with organic sugarcane. . Apologue Celery Root Herbal Liqueur is made by a Chicago-based company which features regional ingredients from independent farmers. In addition to celery root, ingredients include anise seed, celery stalk, cinchona bark, dill, fennel seed, lemon peel, summer savory, and tarragon. It is sweetened with organic sugarcane.', FALSE, '2025-02-24', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/55f8e440-7f53-0137-a906-0afceed97cce/apologue_celery_root_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100145, 'DeGroff Bitter Aperitivo', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 25, 'This American-made bitter aperitivo was made in collaboration with chemist & absinthe distiller T.A. "Ted" Breaux and the Cocktail King himself, Dale DeGroff. Distilled by the team at Clear Creek Distillery in Oregon, this is made with a blend of botanicals including fruits, roots, flowers, and leaves, but no artificial ingredients or colors. Available early May 2023. (SRP $29. This American-made bitter aperitivo was made in collaboration with chemist & absinthe distiller T.A. "Ted" Breaux and the Cocktail King himself, Dale DeGroff. Distilled by the team at Clear Creek Distillery in Oregon, this is made with a blend of botanicals including fruits, roots, flowers, and leaves, but no artificial ingredients or colors. Available early May 2023. (SRP $29.99 for 700ml)', FALSE, '2025-01-13', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/9e970e60-b656-013b-08d5-12aa63fb4bcb/degroff_aperitivo_original-1680852150.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101364, 'Campari Cask Tales (Discontinued)', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 25, 'Created by Campari Group’s herbalist and master blender Bruno Malavasi, Campari Cask Tales was first released in Europe in 2018 and made its debut Stateside the following year. The brand’s famed ruby-hued amaro is finished in used bourbon barrels before being bottled at 25% ABV. Created by Campari Group’s herbalist and master blender Bruno Malavasi, Campari Cask Tales was first released in Europe in 2018 and made its debut Stateside the following year. The brand’s famed ruby-hued amaro is finished in used bourbon barrels before being bottled at 25% ABV. The spirit was created with guidance from top US-based bartenders, including Leo Robitschek, gaz regan and Jeffrey Morgenthaler.', FALSE, '2025-02-08', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/492431e0-e3e3-0137-3914-56675530fea8/campari_cask_tales_original.?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100551, 'Don Ciccio & Figli Ambrosia', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 15, 'Don Ciccio & Figli Ambrosia is an aperitivo crafted in Washington D.C. The bittersweet liqueur is made using all-natural ingredients such as turmeric, carrots, blood orange (from Florida), cantelope (from Virginia), and 9 botanicals sourced from Italy. The recipe dates back to 1908, from founder Francesco Amodeo''s family. Don Ciccio & Figli Ambrosia is an aperitivo crafted in Washington D.C. The bittersweet liqueur is made using all-natural ingredients such as turmeric, carrots, blood orange (from Florida), cantelope (from Virginia), and 9 botanicals sourced from Italy. The recipe dates back to 1908, from founder Francesco Amodeo''s family.', FALSE, '2025-02-28', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/ca9e5be0-5972-0137-e1c4-662d7bd8cc56/don_ciccio_figli_ambrosia_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100290, 'Grand Marnier Cuvée Louis Alexandre', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Grand Marnier Cuvée Louis Alexandre is a premium orange liqueur named for Louis-Alexandre Marnier Lapostolle. In 1880, he''s said to have come up with the idea to blend a cognac with an orange liqueur, turning that concept into a huge success eventually named Grand Marnier. His namesake release is comprised of VSOP cognac (82%) which aged in a mix of Tronçais and Limousin French oak and Liqueur d''orange (18%). Bottled at 40% ABV, it is available in limited quantities beginning March 2019. Grand Marnier Cuvée Louis Alexandre is a premium orange liqueur named for Louis-Alexandre Marnier Lapostolle. In 1880, he''s said to have come up with the idea to blend a cognac with an orange liqueur, turning that concept into a huge success eventually named Grand Marnier. His namesake release is comprised of VSOP cognac (82%) which aged in a mix of Tronçais and Limousin French oak and Liqueur d''orange (18%). Bottled at 40% ABV, it is available in limited quantities beginning March 2019.', FALSE, '2025-01-24', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/87105660-1ebb-0137-dceb-02d8a49d8bf0/grand_marnier_cuvee_louis_alexandre_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100712, 'Five Farms Irish Cream Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Ireland', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 17, 'Five Farms is produced in County Cork, Ireland using small batches of dairy cream sourced from local farms. It is then blended with Irish whiskey, more than is typically used in an Irish cream. It is bottled in packaging reminiscent of vintage milk bottles at 34 proof. . Five Farms is produced in County Cork, Ireland using small batches of dairy cream sourced from local farms. It is then blended with Irish whiskey, more than is typically used in an Irish cream. It is bottled in packaging reminiscent of vintage milk bottles at 34 proof.', FALSE, '2025-01-23', 'Cream', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/8ac0cde0-f90b-0136-52bc-7aea25f584cf/fivefarms_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101276, 'Long Road Distillers Amaro Pazzo', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 28.5, 'Amaro Pazzo is made Long Road Distillers, a grain to glass distillery located in Grand Rapids, Michigan. The base of the amaro is made from 100% winter wheat grown by neighboring Heffron Farms. The spirit is infused with wormwood, gentian, chicory, orange peel, myrrh, and other botanicals. Then it is blended with coffee from Madcap Coffee which is also based in Grand Rapids. Amaro Pazzo is made Long Road Distillers, a grain to glass distillery located in Grand Rapids, Michigan. The base of the amaro is made from 100% winter wheat grown by neighboring Heffron Farms. The spirit is infused with wormwood, gentian, chicory, orange peel, myrrh, and other botanicals. Then it is blended with coffee from Madcap Coffee which is also based in Grand Rapids.', FALSE, '2025-02-09', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/9deefc40-f295-0136-03ff-16899281504d/amaro_pazzo_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100404, 'Grand Brulot', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Made on an estate in Cognac, France, this liqueur blends 6-year-old VSOP cognac made from ugni blanc and colombard grapes with 100% Robusta coffee beans from Ecuador. Before being bottled at 80 proof, the blend is finished in French oak barrels. Made on an estate in Cognac, France, this liqueur blends 6-year-old VSOP cognac made from ugni blanc and colombard grapes with 100% Robusta coffee beans from Ecuador. Before being bottled at 80 proof, the blend is finished in French oak barrels. Grand Brulot’s name refers to a drink called The Brulôt, a blend of coffee and cognac that purportedly dates back nearly two centuries.', FALSE, '2025-02-17', 'Coffee', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/c41ba380-e2f5-0136-1376-421cecac808a/grand_brulot_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101204, 'Mathilde Cassis Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 16, 'Mathilde Cassis Liqueur is made with two varieties of black currants from the Burgundy region: Noir de Bourgogne and Blackdown. The fruit is infused in liquor for a lengthy period of time and is then bottled at 16 percent ABV. Mathilde Cassis Liqueur is made with two varieties of black currants from the Burgundy region: Noir de Bourgogne and Blackdown. The fruit is infused in liquor for a lengthy period of time and is then bottled at 16 percent ABV. Cassis is essential in a variety of classic cocktails like the Kir Royale and the Diablo.', FALSE, '2025-02-15', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/f35e3ac0-ce6d-0136-ea06-4e63380ab660/mathilde_cassis_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100648, 'Tattersall Crème de Fleur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 30, 'Tattersall Crème de Fleur is made in Minneapolis, MN with six different aromatic flowers in the distillation process. Additionally, a further mix of flowers is added to the liqueur post-distillation. Tattersall Crème de Fleur is made in Minneapolis, MN with six different aromatic flowers in the distillation process. Additionally, a further mix of flowers is added to the liqueur post-distillation. Bottled at 60 proof.', FALSE, '2025-02-01', 'Floral', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/05c48a50-5986-0137-bc75-62eb924a007d/tattersall_creme_de_fleur_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100247, 'Campari', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 24, 'Campari was created circa 1860 by a Lombardy-born man named Gaspare Campari. He worked his way up to barman in a cafe in Torino before moving to Milano where he created his renowned bitter concoction. His namesake bitters was first known as Bitter all’usa d’Holanda and its ingredients have never been disclosed other than to say that “it is the result of an infusion of bitter herbs, aromatic plants, and fruit in alcohol and water”. The only other change to the original recipe occured in 2006 when carmine (a natural dye sourced from crushed cochineal insects) ceased to be used for coloring. Campari was created circa 1860 by a Lombardy-born man named Gaspare Campari. He worked his way up to barman in a cafe in Torino before moving to Milano where he created his renowned bitter concoction. His namesake bitters was first known as Bitter all’usa d’Holanda and its ingredients have never been disclosed other than to say that “it is the result of an infusion of bitter herbs, aromatic plants, and fruit in alcohol and water”. The only other change to the original recipe occured in 2006 when carmine (a natural dye sourced from crushed cochineal insects) ceased to be used for coloring. Now artificial colors are used.', FALSE, '2025-01-12', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/09c34bd0-d4d7-0136-c521-326b08ee4111/campari_original-1702505057.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100698, 'Apologue Aronia Berry Liqueur', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 24, 'Apologue Aronia Berry Liqueur is made by a Chicago-based company which features regional ingredients from independent farmers. Aside from aronia berries, ingredients include bitter orange peel, cinnamon, lavender flower, lemon peel, orange peel, orris root, raspberry, rose hip, sweet ashlock prune, and tart cherry. It is sweetened with organic sugarcane. . Apologue Aronia Berry Liqueur is made by a Chicago-based company which features regional ingredients from independent farmers. Aside from aronia berries, ingredients include bitter orange peel, cinnamon, lavender flower, lemon peel, orange peel, orris root, raspberry, rose hip, sweet ashlock prune, and tart cherry. It is sweetened with organic sugarcane.', FALSE, '2025-01-08', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/48503770-7f54-0137-a907-0afceed97cce/apologue_aronia_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101414, 'Copper & Kings Destillaré Intense Chocolat', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 45, 'Introduced to its line of Destillarè liqueurs in 2019, Copper & Kings Destillaré Intense Chocolat is made by adding Caribbean cocoa nibs to a barrel filled with the distillery’s signature American Brandy. This mixture is then allowed to aged for an additional six to nine months. Before being bottled at 90 proof, the liqueur is diluted with reverse osmosis filtered water steeped with cocoa nibs and then sweetened with honey. . Introduced to its line of Destillarè liqueurs in 2019, Copper & Kings Destillaré Intense Chocolat is made by adding Caribbean cocoa nibs to a barrel filled with the distillery’s signature American Brandy. This mixture is then allowed to aged for an additional six to nine months. Before being bottled at 90 proof, the liqueur is diluted with reverse osmosis filtered water steeped with cocoa nibs and then sweetened with honey.', FALSE, '2025-01-22', 'Chocolate', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/a62ee6c0-60bd-0137-3eee-2e47ef323572/destillare_intense_chocolat_liqueur_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100877, 'Don Ciccio & Figli C3 Carciofo', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 23, 'C3 Carciofo is a bitter artichoke liqueur based on a traditional Italian recipe dating to 1911. The core of the aperitivo, and its namesake, are the three types of California-grown artichokes used in production, along with cardoons, grapefruit, and 18 botanicals. C3 Carciofo is a bitter artichoke liqueur based on a traditional Italian recipe dating to 1911. The core of the aperitivo, and its namesake, are the three types of California-grown artichokes used in production, along with cardoons, grapefruit, and 18 botanicals. C3 Carciofo is barrel aged for 12 months and then bottled at 23% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-01-09', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/b26ec340-f453-0136-e462-02ef15e91c73/don_ciccio_figli_amaro_c3_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100673, 'Amaro Nonino Quintessentia', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 35, '"Quintessentia" represents the perfect tweak of a family amaro recipe that''s been passed down through generations. The base of the liqueur is the distillery''s own grappa matured in various European oak casks. This spirit is then infused with an undisclosed blend of herbs and botanicals. . "Quintessentia" represents the perfect tweak of a family amaro recipe that''s been passed down through generations. The base of the liqueur is the distillery''s own grappa matured in various European oak casks. This spirit is then infused with an undisclosed blend of herbs and botanicals.', FALSE, '2025-02-17', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/eb8930d0-e639-0136-d297-526365eea40c/amaronino_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100187, 'Chartreuse Yellow Liqueur', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Yellow Chartreuse is milder and sweeter than the Green version. Introduced in 1838, this liqueur is made from 130 herbs, plants and flowers which were crushed, macerated, and distilled in a manner which is known its entirety by two monks today. All natural color with no preservatives added, its color is derived from maceration. Bottled at 80 proof. Yellow Chartreuse is milder and sweeter than the Green version. Introduced in 1838, this liqueur is made from 130 herbs, plants and flowers which were crushed, macerated, and distilled in a manner which is known its entirety by two monks today. All natural color with no preservatives added, its color is derived from maceration. Bottled at 80 proof.', FALSE, '2025-02-05', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/178f88b0-e565-0136-9210-2657365a3cd8/yellow_chartreuse_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100375, 'Licor 43', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Spain', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 31, 'Inspired by the ancient Roman recipe for Liqvor Mirabilis, a golden-hued liqueur infused with fruits and herbs, Licor 43 was first bottled to sell in the 1940s by siblings Diego, Angel and Josefina Zamora. It caught on throughout Spain, where it’s still a mainstay in bars and often mixed with milk or soda. Though its recipe is a tightly guarded secret, its name does reference the 43 ingredients that give it its unique flavor, including citrus, vanilla, and a variety of aromatic herbs and spices. . Inspired by the ancient Roman recipe for Liqvor Mirabilis, a golden-hued liqueur infused with fruits and herbs, Licor 43 was first bottled to sell in the 1940s by siblings Diego, Angel and Josefina Zamora. It caught on throughout Spain, where it’s still a mainstay in bars and often mixed with milk or soda. Though its recipe is a tightly guarded secret, its name does reference the 43 ingredients that give it its unique flavor, including citrus, vanilla, and a variety of aromatic herbs and spices.', FALSE, '2025-02-10', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/31b1b370-e227-0136-50d3-1a64d39bf23a/licor_43_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100764, 'Rieger''s Caffe Amaro', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 31, 'A collaboration with Kansas City''s J. Rieger & Co. and Thou Mayest Coffee Roaster, this coffee-flavored, Italian-style amaro blends flavors from a Sumatran single origin coffee beans with botanicals and herbs like juniper berries, anise, cardamom, orange peel, spearmint, and vanilla. It then spends a short time in a whiskey barrel to develop its unique flavor before being sweetened with cane syrup. While a dram of this is not akin to sipping a cup of your morning joe, this amaro does contain about 467mg of caffeine per bottle. . A collaboration with Kansas City''s J. Rieger & Co. and Thou Mayest Coffee Roaster, this coffee-flavored, Italian-style amaro blends flavors from a Sumatran single origin coffee beans with botanicals and herbs like juniper berries, anise, cardamom, orange peel, spearmint, and vanilla. It then spends a short time in a whiskey barrel to develop its unique flavor before being sweetened with cane syrup. While a dram of this is not akin to sipping a cup of your morning joe, this amaro does contain about 467mg of caffeine per bottle.', FALSE, '2025-02-20', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/8fe3d5d0-e09a-0136-7dc4-4a91e8cb8376/j_rieger_caffe_amaro_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101480, 'Ramazzotti Amaro', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 30, 'Ramazzotti Amaro was created in 1815 by Ausano Ramazzotti who owned an herbalist shop in Milano. The bitter liqueur includes 33 herbs and roots including angelica root, bitter orange, cardamom, clove, galangal, myrrh, rose petals, star anise, sweet orange, and vanilla. Ausano opened up a cafe near La Scala theater where his customers could consume his amaro instead of coffee. Although it was crafted in Milan, it is now produced in Canelli, Piemonte. Ramazzotti Amaro was created in 1815 by Ausano Ramazzotti who owned an herbalist shop in Milano. The bitter liqueur includes 33 herbs and roots including angelica root, bitter orange, cardamom, clove, galangal, myrrh, rose petals, star anise, sweet orange, and vanilla. Ausano opened up a cafe near La Scala theater where his customers could consume his amaro instead of coffee. Although it was crafted in Milan, it is now produced in Canelli, Piemonte.', FALSE, '2025-01-26', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/b3044250-c370-0136-3451-36f24f087537/ramazzotti_amaro_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101178, 'Cynar', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 16.5, 'Pronounced chee-nar, this Italian digestivo first hit the Italian market in the 1950s. Cynar was founded by Venetian entrepreneur Angelo Valle Molle and is distilled from a blend of 13 herbs, as well as artichoke leaves—the star ingredient from which the amaro gets its name. The unique moniker, which often stumps drinkers, comes from cynarin, a property found in artichokes, and likely also for the vegetable’s botanical name, Cynara scolymus. It is bottled at 16. Pronounced chee-nar, this Italian digestivo first hit the Italian market in the 1950s. Cynar was founded by Venetian entrepreneur Angelo Valle Molle and is distilled from a blend of 13 herbs, as well as artichoke leaves—the star ingredient from which the amaro gets its name. The unique moniker, which often stumps drinkers, comes from cynarin, a property found in artichokes, and likely also for the vegetable’s botanical name, Cynara scolymus. It is bottled at 16.5% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-01-13', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/ef0516e0-ba02-0136-c24a-5e719d11731e/cynar_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101290, 'Copper & Kings Destillaré Intense Orange Curaçao', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 45, 'Brandy is Copper & Kings’ bread and butter, so it comes as no surprise that the brand’s liqueur would use a base of apple brandy low wine, or the spirit from the first round of distillation. To make the orange curaçao, the apple brandy goes through a process of multiple macerations and distillations with orange peels, spices, honey, and lavender before being finished in the brand’s own brandy barrels for three to six months. The spirit is then sweetened and cut with orange blossom honey. It is bottled at 45% ABV. Brandy is Copper & Kings’ bread and butter, so it comes as no surprise that the brand’s liqueur would use a base of apple brandy low wine, or the spirit from the first round of distillation. To make the orange curaçao, the apple brandy goes through a process of multiple macerations and distillations with orange peels, spices, honey, and lavender before being finished in the brand’s own brandy barrels for three to six months. The spirit is then sweetened and cut with orange blossom honey. It is bottled at 45% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-02-28', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/91c610e0-b947-0136-1f42-064fa7daa725/copper_kings_destillare_orange_curacao_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101095, 'Chambord Liqueur', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 16.5, 'Chambord Liqueur is a black raspberry liqueur. It is made from an infusion of raspberries and blackberries. Other ingredients include Madagascar vanilla, Moroccan citrus peel, honey, and XO cognac which the master blender balances all together to create a concentrate. Although this French liqueur is based on a recipe from the late 17th century, it wasn''t released commercially until 1981. Bottled at 16.5% ABV. Chambord Liqueur is a black raspberry liqueur. It is made from an infusion of raspberries and blackberries. Other ingredients include Madagascar vanilla, Moroccan citrus peel, honey, and XO cognac which the master blender balances all together to create a concentrate. Although this French liqueur is based on a recipe from the late 17th century, it wasn''t released commercially until 1981. Bottled at 16.5% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-01-09', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/46319c10-b881-0136-a860-567b4010a2cb/chambord_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100692, 'Cointreau', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Cointreau is a clear, orange flavored liqueur developed in 1875 by Édouard Cointreau, son of one of the co-founding brothers of the distillery. In 1885 it became the first registered brand of triple sec, although the brand dropped "triple sec" from its name in early 20th century.  It is made with both bitter and sweet orange peels which are macerated in neutral alcohol and then distilled. The only other ingredients are sugar and water. Suitable for any recipe calling for triple sec. Note: As February 2023, Cointreau has redesigned the bottle to celebrate the orange, its key ingredient, more prominently. The new label also has a QR code granting consumers access to almost 500 drinks. . Cointreau is a clear, orange flavored liqueur developed in 1875 by Édouard Cointreau, son of one of the co-founding brothers of the distillery. In 1885 it became the first registered brand of triple sec, although the brand dropped "triple sec" from its name in early 20th century.  It is made with both bitter and sweet orange peels which are macerated in neutral alcohol and then distilled. The only other ingredients are sugar and water. Suitable for any recipe calling for triple sec. Note: As February 2023, Cointreau has redesigned the bottle to celebrate the orange, its key ingredient, more prominently. The new label also has a QR code granting consumers access to almost 500 drinks.', FALSE, '2025-01-04', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/2f73e040-b6f3-0136-615d-52c2f3914668/cointreau_original-1676504447.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100064, 'Pimm''s No. 1 Cup', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Scotland', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 25, 'Pimm''s No. 1 is the most popular of the liqueur category known as cups. First created in 1840, No. 1 uses gin as its base along with a secret blend of spices, fruit, and botanicals. There have been other Pimm''s over the years; No. 2 had a Scotch base, No. 3 used brandy, No. 4 was rum, No. 5 rye, and No. 6 used Vodka. They have all had been discontinued, but Diageo which currently owns Pimm''s, rebranded No. 3 as Winter''s Cup and it still uses brandy as its base. Every bar, both at home and otherwise, has their own recipe for their perfect Pimm''s Cup cocktail. Some use lemonade, others lemon-lime soda or ginger ale. Pimm''s No. 1 is the most popular of the liqueur category known as cups. First created in 1840, No. 1 uses gin as its base along with a secret blend of spices, fruit, and botanicals. There have been other Pimm''s over the years; No. 2 had a Scotch base, No. 3 used brandy, No. 4 was rum, No. 5 rye, and No. 6 used Vodka. They have all had been discontinued, but Diageo which currently owns Pimm''s, rebranded No. 3 as Winter''s Cup and it still uses brandy as its base. Every bar, both at home and otherwise, has their own recipe for their perfect Pimm''s Cup cocktail. Some use lemonade, others lemon-lime soda or ginger ale. The sky is the limit for fruit additions, but strawberry and cucumber slices are quite common, especially during Wimbledon.', FALSE, '2025-01-23', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/389d9590-719d-0134-cce0-365007cbbf44/pimms_no_1_cup_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100846, 'Mozart Coconut Chocolate Liqueur', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Austria', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 15, 'This expression is produced in the same tradition as the other liqueurs in the brand''s portfolio. It is made with cocoa from West Africa and fair trader vanilla from Madagascar as well as tropical coconut flavors. Though it has a creamy consistency, it is lactose and gluten free. It is bottled at 30 proof. This is a permanent addition to the portfolio and is available in the US beginning July 2024. (SRP $29. This expression is produced in the same tradition as the other liqueurs in the brand''s portfolio. It is made with cocoa from West Africa and fair trader vanilla from Madagascar as well as tropical coconut flavors. Though it has a creamy consistency, it is lactose and gluten free. It is bottled at 30 proof. This is a permanent addition to the portfolio and is available in the US beginning July 2024. (SRP $29.99)', FALSE, '2025-01-23', 'Chocolate', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/56c4da80-277c-013d-f062-62c4d3db95fa/mozart-coconut-chocolate-liqueur_original-1721354036.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100672, 'RumChata Limon', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 14, 'This expression in the RumChata cream liqueur lineup combines Caribbean rum with real dairy cream, vanilla and lemon. It is available as of April, 2021. This expression in the RumChata cream liqueur lineup combines Caribbean rum with real dairy cream, vanilla and lemon. It is available as of April, 2021.', FALSE, '2025-02-22', 'Cream', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/2c802640-7780-0138-db01-6aa85299b368/rumchatalimon_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100246, 'Apologue Persimmon Bittersweet Liqueur', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 27, 'Apologue Persimmon Bittersweet Liqueur is made by a Chicago-based company which features regional ingredients from independent farmers. Aside from the persimmon, ingredients include hibiscus flower, bitter orange peel, orange peel, lemon peel, cinchona bark, gentian root, rhubarb root, ginger root, cinnamon, cardamom, and spearmint. It is sweetened with organic sugarcane. . Apologue Persimmon Bittersweet Liqueur is made by a Chicago-based company which features regional ingredients from independent farmers. Aside from the persimmon, ingredients include hibiscus flower, bitter orange peel, orange peel, lemon peel, cinchona bark, gentian root, rhubarb root, ginger root, cinnamon, cardamom, and spearmint. It is sweetened with organic sugarcane.', FALSE, '2025-02-13', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/023448e0-7f55-0137-2fc2-5a48569bc4cb/apologue_persimmon_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101431, 'Saint Brendan''s Irish Cream', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Ireland', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 17, 'Made in Derry, Northern Ireland, Saint Brendan’s Irish Cream uses a blend of Irish whiskey and fresh cream. The brand claims a higher butterfat content than its counterparts. Made in Derry, Northern Ireland, Saint Brendan’s Irish Cream uses a blend of Irish whiskey and fresh cream. The brand claims a higher butterfat content than its counterparts.', FALSE, '2025-01-19', 'Cream', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/13311960-fcb0-0136-973e-7e49fab3eeb7/saint_brandans_irish_cream_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100798, 'Still Austin Whiskey Co. Delevante Coffee Liqueur', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 25, 'Delevante Coffee Liqueur is made at the Still Austin Whiskey Co., a grain-to-glass distillery in Austin, Texas which uses only Texas-grown grains in their products. Their coffee liqueur uses a corn whiskey as its base and coffee from local coffee roaster Spokesman Coffee. It''s named for the distillery''s master distiller, Michael Delevante. Delevante Coffee Liqueur is made at the Still Austin Whiskey Co., a grain-to-glass distillery in Austin, Texas which uses only Texas-grown grains in their products. Their coffee liqueur uses a corn whiskey as its base and coffee from local coffee roaster Spokesman Coffee. It''s named for the distillery''s master distiller, Michael Delevante.', FALSE, '2025-02-22', 'Coffee', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/bd10f460-f28e-0136-81cb-028de5bc5384/delevante_coffee_liqueur_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100954, 'Martini & Rossi Riserva Speciale Bitter Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 28.5, 'Martini & Rossi''s Riserva Speciale Bitter joined the product family in summer 2017. Inspired by the brand''s original bitter recipe from 1872, the product was crafted to pair with Martini''s Riserva Speciale Vermouth Di Torino in cocktails. In addition to Italian artemesia, the three key botanicals are saffron, angostura and columba. . Martini & Rossi''s Riserva Speciale Bitter joined the product family in summer 2017. Inspired by the brand''s original bitter recipe from 1872, the product was crafted to pair with Martini''s Riserva Speciale Vermouth Di Torino in cocktails. In addition to Italian artemesia, the three key botanicals are saffron, angostura and columba.', FALSE, '2025-02-16', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/abd41040-cc46-0136-5663-020e31d48091/martini_riserva_speciale_bitter_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100292, 'Starlino Rosé Aperitivo', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 17, 'Starlino Rosé Aperitivo is made using Italian wine and its botanicals include pink grapefruit peel, orange peel, elderflower, Italian raspberries and strawberries, coriander, and wormwood among others. It is bottled at 17% ABV. Starlino Rosé Aperitivo is made using Italian wine and its botanicals include pink grapefruit peel, orange peel, elderflower, Italian raspberries and strawberries, coriander, and wormwood among others. It is bottled at 17% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-01-24', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/ffec56f0-e0e2-0138-3ae5-0215098f0b1c/starlino_rose_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100153, 'Blue Lion Chicorée Liqueur', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Made by New Hampshire’s Tamworth Distilling, this 80-proof liqueur is named for the chicory flower, often referred to as a blue dandelion. It channels the bittersweet flavors of Italian amaro, it’s made with chicory root, rye seed, spices, dandelion root and cane sugar. The brand recommends pairing the liqueur with coffee to evoke the classic New Orleans chicory coffee. . Made by New Hampshire’s Tamworth Distilling, this 80-proof liqueur is named for the chicory flower, often referred to as a blue dandelion. It channels the bittersweet flavors of Italian amaro, it’s made with chicory root, rye seed, spices, dandelion root and cane sugar. The brand recommends pairing the liqueur with coffee to evoke the classic New Orleans chicory coffee.', FALSE, '2025-01-12', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/c80aff70-e2f1-0136-8d63-56020b2d7cb7/blue_lion_chicoree_liqueur_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100804, 'The Whistler Irish Cream', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Ireland', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 19, 'The Whistler Irish Cream is one of three releases in the Trilogy Series all crafted by Michael Walsh, master distiller, master blender, and family beekeeper for Boann Distillery which owns the brand. Irish Cream, dubbed The Blenders Select, begins with single pot still whiskey which uses malted and unmalted barley in its makeup. Then Irish cream from grass-fed cows is blended in. This cream liqueur is bottled at 38 proof. The Whistler Irish Cream is one of three releases in the Trilogy Series all crafted by Michael Walsh, master distiller, master blender, and family beekeeper for Boann Distillery which owns the brand. Irish Cream, dubbed The Blenders Select, begins with single pot still whiskey which uses malted and unmalted barley in its makeup. Then Irish cream from grass-fed cows is blended in. This cream liqueur is bottled at 38 proof.', FALSE, '2025-02-20', 'Cream', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/5bfdc3e0-4c37-0138-16bd-0aaafef9a829/the_whistler_irish_cream_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100781, 'Tia Maria Matcha Cream Liqueur', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 17, 'This cream liqueur presents a notable product shift for this brand, known for its coffee liqueurs. It is a cream liqueur with the flavors of matcha green tea, bottled at 17% ABV. It is available as of May, 2021. . This cream liqueur presents a notable product shift for this brand, known for its coffee liqueurs. It is a cream liqueur with the flavors of matcha green tea, bottled at 17% ABV. It is available as of May, 2021.', FALSE, '2025-02-03', 'Cream', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/9712c9e0-958e-0139-6f64-563bb90ec693/tiamaria_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100526, 'Tattersall Bitter Orange', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 28, 'Founded in 2015, Tattersall Distilling Co. makes a host of spirits including whiskey, gin, aquavit, and liqueurs at its Minneapolis distillery. Its Tattersall Bitter Orange is made from three varieties of orange and an undisclosed selection of spices. . Founded in 2015, Tattersall Distilling Co. makes a host of spirits including whiskey, gin, aquavit, and liqueurs at its Minneapolis distillery. Its Tattersall Bitter Orange is made from three varieties of orange and an undisclosed selection of spices.', FALSE, '2025-01-15', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/31230cc0-60b6-0137-9c0c-4e2d9e1ad15b/tattersall_bitter_orange_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100912, 'Mozart Strawberry White Chocolate Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Austria', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 15, 'Mozart Distillerie produces chocolate liqueurs in Salzburg, Austria — birthplace of composer Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart. This Strawberry Chocolate expression is a spring seasonal release made with white chocolate, vanilla, and strawberry flavor. This strawberry pink colored liqueur is gluten free and bottled at 15% ABV. (SRP $29. Mozart Distillerie produces chocolate liqueurs in Salzburg, Austria — birthplace of composer Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart. This Strawberry Chocolate expression is a spring seasonal release made with white chocolate, vanilla, and strawberry flavor. This strawberry pink colored liqueur is gluten free and bottled at 15% ABV. (SRP $29.99 per 750ml)', FALSE, '2025-02-14', 'Chocolate', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/5d9922c0-3803-0137-1f52-3e5c59724f25/mozard_strawberry_chocolate_original-1688675881.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100748, 'Grand Marnier', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Grand Marnier is an orange liqueur made from a blend of cognac (51%) and bitter orange distillate (49%). To make this distillate, the bitter orange variety citrus Bigaradia is harvested and the peels are sun-dried. The peels then macerate in neutral alcohol for ~10 days before it is distilled. This bitter orange distillate is then blended with cognac and further aged in large oak vats for 1-6 months. Originally named Curaçao Marnier when created in 1880 by founder Louis-Alexandre Marnier Lapostolle, it was soon changed to Grand Marnier after friends declared it to be grand. Also called Grand Marnier Cordon Rouge or simply GrandMa by those in the bar industry. Grand Marnier is an orange liqueur made from a blend of cognac (51%) and bitter orange distillate (49%). To make this distillate, the bitter orange variety citrus Bigaradia is harvested and the peels are sun-dried. The peels then macerate in neutral alcohol for ~10 days before it is distilled. This bitter orange distillate is then blended with cognac and further aged in large oak vats for 1-6 months. Originally named Curaçao Marnier when created in 1880 by founder Louis-Alexandre Marnier Lapostolle, it was soon changed to Grand Marnier after friends declared it to be grand. Also called Grand Marnier Cordon Rouge or simply GrandMa by those in the bar industry.', FALSE, '2025-01-07', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/bab33fd0-afe0-0136-084e-66cba29ee39d/grand_marnier_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101498, 'Toschi Nocello Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 24, 'Flavored with both walnuts and hazelnuts, Toschi Nocello is made in Savignano Sul Panaro, Italy. It''s bottled at 24 percent ABV and often comes adorned with an imitation walnut shell secured around the neck of the bottle. Flavored with both walnuts and hazelnuts, Toschi Nocello is made in Savignano Sul Panaro, Italy. It''s bottled at 24 percent ABV and often comes adorned with an imitation walnut shell secured around the neck of the bottle. The brand recommends drinking the nutty liqueur neat, over ice, or in coffee.', FALSE, '2025-01-26', 'Nut', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/9cb90610-ce67-0136-ea01-4e63380ab660/toschi_nocello_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100132, 'Fernet-Vallet', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Mexico', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 35, 'Henri Vallet emigrated from France to Mexico in the mid-1800s, where he then began making a variety of liqueurs unusual to the region, including this 35% ABV fernet. The amalgam of highly aromatic spices, roots and leaves is still made in accordance with Vallet’s original 19th century recipe. Henri Vallet emigrated from France to Mexico in the mid-1800s, where he then began making a variety of liqueurs unusual to the region, including this 35% ABV fernet. The amalgam of highly aromatic spices, roots and leaves is still made in accordance with Vallet’s original 19th century recipe. The bottle of the aperitivo suggests it can be used in cocktails and in cooking.', FALSE, '2025-01-12', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/33adef60-ba08-0136-019e-1a46aa63541c/fernet_vallet_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100106, 'Amaro Sibilla', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 34, 'Amaro Sibilla is made by Distilleria Varnelli in Le Marche region of Italy. First created in 1868, it is made from a mix of herbs, roots, and barks "prepared over a wood fire. Amaro Sibilla is made by Distilleria Varnelli in Le Marche region of Italy. First created in 1868, it is made from a mix of herbs, roots, and barks "prepared over a wood fire." It is sweetened with honey then aged and decanted before bottling at 34% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-02-20', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/4625f4a0-d418-0136-65b1-7e2383dffb93/sibilla_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100717, 'Patrón XO Cafe', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Mexico', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 35, 'Patrón XO Cafe is a coffee liqueur made with Patrón Silver, a 100% blue agave tequila, and Arabica coffee beans sourced from Veracruz and Chiapas. Typically, neutral spirits or rum are used when making coffee liqueurs. It is bottled at 35% ABV. Note: In October 2021, Patrón announced it was discontinuing this product to focus on its core tequila line and other super and ultra-premium offerings. However, the brand has re-released the product for a one-time limited nationwide release as of April 2024. (SRP $42. Patrón XO Cafe is a coffee liqueur made with Patrón Silver, a 100% blue agave tequila, and Arabica coffee beans sourced from Veracruz and Chiapas. Typically, neutral spirits or rum are used when making coffee liqueurs. It is bottled at 35% ABV. Note: In October 2021, Patrón announced it was discontinuing this product to focus on its core tequila line and other super and ultra-premium offerings. However, the brand has re-released the product for a one-time limited nationwide release as of April 2024. (SRP $42.99)', FALSE, '2025-01-03', 'Coffee', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/84279560-d5bb-0136-5537-7e048e57ef8d/patron_xo_cafe_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100093, 'Rothman & Winter Crème de Violette', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Austria', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 20, 'Made with a base of brandy, this liqueur gets its flavor from Queen Charlotte and March violets found in the Alps. No additional fruit or spice flavors are added to the liqueur before it’s bottled at 20% ABV. It is recommended that this liqueur is used within two years of purchase. . Made with a base of brandy, this liqueur gets its flavor from Queen Charlotte and March violets found in the Alps. No additional fruit or spice flavors are added to the liqueur before it’s bottled at 20% ABV. It is recommended that this liqueur is used within two years of purchase.', FALSE, '2025-02-07', 'Floral', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/975326f0-ba05-0136-7f35-1ef466691924/crem_de_violette_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100243, 'Zucca Rabarbaro', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 30, 'The recipe for Zucca Rabarbaro dates back to 1845 when a doctor prescribed rhubarb and medicinal herbs to Tilde Zucca to aid her digestion. Her husband Ettore decided to add alcohol to the concoction. It became quite popular in cafes as an aperitif in Milan among other European cities. In the early 1900s, a descendant of Ettore, Carlo, established the Zucca Company to bring the product to shelves. Rabarbaro is Italian for "rhubarb" and is the only disclosed ingredient by the brand. The rhubarb root is sourced from the Gansu province in China. Note: In Spring 2016, this product got an updated label and recipe upping the proof from 30 to 60. . The recipe for Zucca Rabarbaro dates back to 1845 when a doctor prescribed rhubarb and medicinal herbs to Tilde Zucca to aid her digestion. Her husband Ettore decided to add alcohol to the concoction. It became quite popular in cafes as an aperitif in Milan among other European cities. In the early 1900s, a descendant of Ettore, Carlo, established the Zucca Company to bring the product to shelves.  Rabarbaro is Italian for "rhubarb" and is the only disclosed ingredient by the brand. The rhubarb root is sourced from the Gansu province in China. Note: In Spring 2016, this product got an updated label and recipe upping the proof from 30 to 60.', FALSE, '2025-01-12', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/aed31410-c1f0-0136-def9-666d7724f0c2/zucca_rabarbaro_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100295, 'Traverse City Whiskey Co. Harvest Cream', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 17, 'This bourbon cream liqueur is made with Traverse City''s XXX Straight Bourbon. Enjoy on the rocks or mixed in coffee or cocktails. Bottled at 17% ABV, it''s available for the holiday season beginning November 2023. (SRP $27. This bourbon cream liqueur is made with Traverse City''s XXX Straight Bourbon. Enjoy on the rocks or mixed in coffee or cocktails. Bottled at 17% ABV, it''s available for the holiday season beginning November 2023. (SRP $27.99)', FALSE, '2025-01-01', 'Cream', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/ffda6b20-662f-013c-3f58-2aa1a414bebf/traverse-city-whiskey-co-harvest-cream_original-1700169965.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100725, 'Maggie''s Farm Falernum Liqueur', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 25, 'Allegheny Distilling located in Pittsburgh, PA is the maker of Maggie’s Farm Rum. In addition to its impressive roster of rum, the distillery produces a rum-based Falernum Liqueur. Made from a base of Maggie’s Farm White Rum, it’s flavored with ginger, lime zest, and toasted whole cloves and allspice berries. The liqueur is then sweetened with Louisiana turbinado sugar and bottled at 25% ABV. Allegheny Distilling located in Pittsburgh, PA is the maker of Maggie’s Farm Rum. In addition to its impressive roster of rum, the distillery produces a rum-based Falernum Liqueur. Made from a base of Maggie’s Farm White Rum, it’s flavored with ginger, lime zest, and toasted whole cloves and allspice berries. The liqueur is then sweetened with Louisiana turbinado sugar and bottled at 25% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-01-15', 'Other', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/ce259ce0-024f-0137-973c-5e35cc903303/maggies_falernum_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100799, 'Luxardo Fernet Amaro', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Although best known for the brand''s Maraschino Liqueur, Luxardo makes a host of liqueurs and bitters including this Fernet Amaro. It is made from a recipe which features 15 different herbs, spices and botanicals including cardamom, gentian, licorice, and saffron. Although best known for the brand''s Maraschino Liqueur, Luxardo makes a host of liqueurs and bitters including this Fernet Amaro. It is made from a recipe which features 15 different herbs, spices and botanicals including cardamom, gentian, licorice, and saffron.', FALSE, '2025-01-23', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/45f307c0-da51-0136-a520-522bdc746943/luxardo_fernet_amaro_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100552, 'Tattersall Fernet', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 35, 'Founded in 2015, Tattersall Distilling Co. based in Minneapolis makes a host of spirits including whiskey, gin, aquavit, and liqueurs. The distillery''s fernet is made with over 30 botanicals, herbs, and spices. Bottled at 70 proof. Founded in 2015, Tattersall Distilling Co. based in Minneapolis makes a host of spirits including whiskey, gin, aquavit, and liqueurs. The distillery''s fernet is made with over 30 botanicals, herbs, and spices. Bottled at 70 proof.', FALSE, '2025-02-19', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/70574b60-30e7-0137-6cac-0260d17cb55c/tattersall_fernet_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101086, 'Salers Gentiane Aperitif', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 16, 'Salers Gentiane Aperitif is made from the root of gentian (Gentiane luta) sourced from the Auvergne region in France. It is lightly sweet and has an all-natural pale straw color. Salers Gentiane Aperitif is made from the root of gentian (Gentiane luta) sourced from the Auvergne region in France. It is lightly sweet and has an all-natural pale straw color. First produced in 1885, this bitter gentian liqueur is bottled at 32 proof.', FALSE, '2025-01-08', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/c5fd8430-dd8e-0136-46f0-524561623431/salers_aperitif_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100829, 'Nixta Licor de Elote', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Mexico', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 30, 'Nixta is billed as the world''s first corn liqueur. It''s made by the team behind Abasolo, a Mexican whisky made from ancestral corn, at the Destilería y Bodega Abasolo in Jilotepec de Abasolo. Nixta uses the ancient process for which it''s named, nixtamalization, to derive flavor from its base of 100% non-GMO Cacahuazintle maíz. It''s bottled at 30% ABV. Nixta is billed as the world''s first corn liqueur. It''s made by the team behind Abasolo, a Mexican whisky made from ancestral corn, at the Destilería y Bodega Abasolo in Jilotepec de Abasolo. Nixta uses the ancient process for which it''s named, nixtamalization, to derive flavor from its base of 100% non-GMO Cacahuazintle maíz. It''s bottled at 30% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-01-11', 'Other', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/4a6dd440-dad7-0138-994b-7efeb4069506/nixtia_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100313, 'Casa D''Aristi Kalani Coconut Rum Liqueur', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Mexico', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 30, 'Made in Mexico’s Yucatan Peninsula, Kalani [kuh-lahn-ee] gets its color and flavor from Yellow Dwarf Coconuts that are harvested at a 19th century colonial plantation. These coconuts are shredded and pressed for milk. Made in Mexico’s Yucatan Peninsula, Kalani [kuh-lahn-ee] gets its color and flavor from Yellow Dwarf Coconuts that are harvested at a 19th century colonial plantation. These coconuts are shredded and pressed for milk. Casa D’Aristi then ferments the coconut milk and macerates it in pure sugar cane rum to create this 60-proof coconut rum liqueur.', FALSE, '2025-01-31', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/5d73fc80-5fec-0137-e2c6-7671b070dcf1/kalani_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101076, 'Kerrygold Irish Cream', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Ireland', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 17, 'Kerrygold Irish Cream Liqueur is made in Ireland from cream from grass-fed cows, Irish whiskey, real chocolate, and "Irish spirit. " It is made from the same milk used to create the brand''s cheese and butter. Kerrygold Irish Cream Liqueur is made in Ireland from cream from grass-fed cows, Irish whiskey, real chocolate, and "Irish spirit." It is made from the same milk used to create the brand''s cheese and butter. First introduced in 2014, it is bottled at 17% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-02-21', 'Cream', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/aea33be0-d7dc-0136-c5c9-16de00be67ce/kerrygold_irish_cream_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100050, 'Amargo Vallet Angostura', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Mexico', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 45, 'The recipe for this bitter liqueur was created by Monsieur Henri Vallet who emigrated to Mexico from France in the mid 1800s. It is made from Angostura bark as well as rhubarb, quassia wood, clove, gentian root, and cherry fruit among other roots and spices. It is bottled at 90 proof. Amargo, means "bitter" in Spanish as does "amaro" in Italian. The recipe for this bitter liqueur was created by Monsieur Henri Vallet who emigrated to Mexico from France in the mid 1800s. It is made from Angostura bark as well as rhubarb, quassia wood, clove, gentian root, and cherry fruit among other roots and spices. It is bottled at 90 proof. Amargo, means "bitter" in Spanish as does "amaro" in Italian.', FALSE, '2025-02-11', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/99dfaef0-c1f5-0136-defe-666d7724f0c2/amargo_vallet_angostura_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100508, 'Mister Katz''s Rock & Rye', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 32.5, 'Rock & Rye was a popular concoction in American bars in the late 19th and early 20th century, masking what was often cheap rye with rock candy and sometimes citrus peels and ginger. In this updated iteration from NY Distilling in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, Mister Katz (Master Distiller Allen Katz) takes a younger version of their Ragtime Rye and mixes it with rock candy made with sugar from the local In the Raw sugar factory and an infusion of botanicals such as dried orange peel, dried Bing cherry, cinnamon, and other spices. Rock & Rye was a popular concoction in American bars in the late 19th and early 20th century, masking what was often cheap rye with rock candy and sometimes citrus peels and ginger. In this updated iteration from NY Distilling in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, Mister Katz (Master Distiller Allen Katz) takes a younger version of their Ragtime Rye and mixes it with rock candy made with sugar from the local In the Raw sugar factory and an infusion of botanicals such as dried orange peel, dried Bing cherry, cinnamon, and other spices.', FALSE, '2025-01-18', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/ea2fbcf0-e609-0133-0555-66385cf1928e/mister_katz_rock_rye_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100474, 'DeGroff New World Amaro', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 35, 'This American-made amaro was made in collaboration with chemist & absinthe distiller T.A. "Ted" Breaux and the Cocktail King himself, Dale DeGroff. Distilled by the team at Clear Creek Distillery in Oregon, this is a West Indies-inspired amaro made with a blend of botanicals including Caribbean spices, fruits, roots, flowers, and leaves, but no artificial ingredients or colors. Available early May 2023. (SRP $39. This American-made amaro was made in collaboration with chemist & absinthe distiller T.A. "Ted" Breaux and the Cocktail King himself, Dale DeGroff. Distilled by the team at Clear Creek Distillery in Oregon, this is a West Indies-inspired amaro made with a blend of botanicals including Caribbean spices, fruits, roots, flowers, and leaves, but no artificial ingredients or colors. Available early May 2023. (SRP $39.99 for 700ml)', FALSE, '2025-01-03', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/c28f3270-b656-013b-cf5d-3e649873b598/degroff_amaro_original-1680852141.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101265, 'Vigo Amaro', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 32.5, 'Vigo Amaro made its debut in 2019 from Philadelphia Distilling. Head distiller Aaron Selya has worked on its creation for four years, and was formulating his recipe even prior to his work with the distillery. The amaro is double macerated with a proprietary blend of botanicals designed to meld tradition with new world innovation. Vigo is named for Francis Vigo, an Italian financier who supported the colonial cause during the Revolutionary War. Vigo Amaro made its debut in 2019 from Philadelphia Distilling. Head distiller Aaron Selya has worked on its creation for four years, and was formulating his recipe even prior to his work with the distillery. The amaro is double macerated with a proprietary blend of botanicals designed to meld tradition with new world innovation. Vigo is named for Francis Vigo, an Italian financier who supported the colonial cause during the Revolutionary War.', FALSE, '2025-01-30', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/7a1419b0-8d9d-0137-0f76-42e6dfdf20e2/vigo_amaro_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100359, 'Lyon Coffee Rum Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 36, 'Maryland’s Lyon Distilling Co. has added a variety of spirits to its roster since it opened in 2013, from white and dark rum to rye whiskey. Launched in 2018, their flagship liqueur uses rum as a base and is infused with coffee from a local roaster. Before being bottled at 72 proof, it’s sweetened with a touch of chocolate. Maryland’s Lyon Distilling Co. has added a variety of spirits to its roster since it opened in 2013, from white and dark rum to rye whiskey. Launched in 2018, their flagship liqueur uses rum as a base and is infused with coffee from a local roaster. Before being bottled at 72 proof, it’s sweetened with a touch of chocolate.', FALSE, '2025-02-02', 'Coffee', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/4b802f70-0310-0137-9fe2-6a95b16a9d36/lyon_coffee_rum_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100130, 'Nooku Bourbon Cream', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 17, 'Nooku Bourbon Cream is made with two ingredients: dairy cream and bourbon from Old Elk Distillery that''s aged for two years. The brand prides itself on foregoing the use of artificial coloring, flavoring, or added sugar and bottles the liqueur at 17% ABV. In addition to Nooku''s original flavor, it also comes in Peppermint and Hot Chocolate varieties. . Nooku Bourbon Cream is made with two ingredients: dairy cream and bourbon from Old Elk Distillery that''s aged for two years. The brand prides itself on foregoing the use of artificial coloring, flavoring, or added sugar and bottles the liqueur at 17% ABV. In addition to Nooku''s original flavor, it also comes in Peppermint and Hot Chocolate varieties.', FALSE, '2025-02-02', 'Cream', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/816b2460-f75a-0136-5531-2288398809b0/nooku_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100073, 'Paula''s Texas Orange Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Paula''s Texas Orange Liqueur is made from a corn spirit which is infused with fresh fruit and pure cane sugar. it is finished with Texas Hill Country rainwater to bring it to 80 proof. It is gluten free and all natural. It was launched in 2005 and is named for brand owner and creator, Paula Angerstein, the first woman and only the second person to be licensed to distill spirits in the state of Texas. Paula''s Texas Orange Liqueur is made from a corn spirit which is infused with fresh fruit and pure cane sugar. it is finished with Texas Hill Country rainwater to bring it to 80 proof. It is gluten free and all natural. It was launched in 2005 and is named for brand owner and creator, Paula Angerstein, the first woman and only the second person to be licensed to distill spirits in the state of Texas.', FALSE, '2025-01-20', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/7f225350-dd76-0136-9b10-561f8738e82c/paulas_texas_orange_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100579, 'Italicus Rosolio di Bergamotto', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 20, 'Italicus Rosolio di Bergamotto is a straw colored citrus liqueur. It was crafted by acclaimed barman and Italian spirits expert Giuseppe Gallo who adjusted the proportions and sweetness levels from a 19th century recipe for Rosolio. It begins with Calabrian bergamot oranges and Sicilian cedri which have gone through the sfumatura process --  a method of extracting essential oils from citrus fruit. This is then added to neutral grain alcohol. Other ingredients include lavender, roses, chamomile, melissa balm and gentian in addition to sugar. . Italicus Rosolio di Bergamotto is a straw colored citrus liqueur. It was crafted by acclaimed barman and Italian spirits expert Giuseppe Gallo who adjusted the proportions and sweetness levels from a 19th century recipe for Rosolio. It begins with Calabrian bergamot oranges and Sicilian cedri which have gone through the sfumatura process --  a method of extracting essential oils from citrus fruit. This is then added to neutral grain alcohol. Other ingredients include lavender, roses, chamomile, melissa balm and gentian in addition to sugar.', FALSE, '2025-02-23', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/9f297eb0-b93f-0136-fe06-6acae6ea3eee/italicus_rosolio_di_bergamotto_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101025, 'Barrow''s Intense Ginger Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 22, 'Barrow''s Intense Ginger Liqueur is made from just four ingredients: fresh ginger, sugar, cane spirit, and filtered water. Made in Brooklyn, NY with no extracts or chemicals this is gluten-free, vegan, and certified kosher. Barrow''s Intense Ginger Liqueur is made from just four ingredients: fresh ginger, sugar, cane spirit, and filtered water. Made in Brooklyn, NY with no extracts or chemicals this is gluten-free, vegan, and certified kosher.', FALSE, '2025-01-26', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/efd85c90-1aab-0137-9f0e-2a4314ad5979/barrows_intense_ginger_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101194, 'Disaronno', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 28, 'Disaronno is an amaretto (almond-flavored liqueur) with a recipe, the brand claims, that dates back to 1525. It was first commercially produced and marketed by the Reina family in the early 20th century in Saronna, just outside of Milano. Originally called Amaretto di Saronno, the iconic square bottle first arrived in 1942. In 2001, the brand dropped Amaretto from its name and is now simply called Disaronno. Disaronno is an amaretto (almond-flavored liqueur) with a recipe, the brand claims, that dates back to 1525. It was first commercially produced and marketed by the Reina family in the early 20th century in Saronna, just outside of Milano. Originally called Amaretto di Saronno, the iconic square bottle first arrived in 1942. In 2001, the brand dropped Amaretto from its name and is now simply called Disaronno.', FALSE, '2025-01-06', 'Nut', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/2d37e050-d5b2-0136-4083-3e28faf1a0ff/disaronno_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100114, 'Cappelletti Amaro Sfumato Rabarbaro', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 20, 'The main ingredient used for this amari is the root of Chinese rabarbaro (rhubarb) which is grown in Trentino-Alto Adige and Veneto. "Sfumato" is Italian for "smoke" which is fitting as Chinese rabarbaro gives off a smoky quality. All production of this amaro is made in house by Luigi & Maddalena Cappelletti, the fourth generation of this distilling family which makes other amari and aromatized wines. . The main ingredient used for this amari is the root of Chinese rabarbaro (rhubarb) which is grown in Trentino-Alto Adige and Veneto. "Sfumato" is Italian for "smoke" which is fitting as Chinese rabarbaro gives off a smoky quality. All production of this amaro is made in house by Luigi & Maddalena Cappelletti, the fourth generation of this distilling family which makes other amari and aromatized wines.', FALSE, '2025-01-21', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/5e9ba970-c397-0136-aa34-12b5018a1cca/cappelletti_amaro_sfumato_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100880, 'Hochstadter''s Slow & Low 100 Proof Rock & Rye', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Multiple Countries', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 50, 'Cooper Spirits follows up their initial Hochstadter''s Slow & Low Rock & Rye, bottled at 84 proof, with this 100 proof edition. While the same flavorings are included, rock candy, raw honey, bitters, and air dried navel oranges, apart from the higher proof another change is in the form of an older whiskey. Cooper Spirits follows up their initial Hochstadter''s Slow & Low Rock & Rye, bottled at 84 proof, with this 100 proof edition. While the same flavorings are included, rock candy, raw honey, bitters, and air dried navel oranges, apart from the higher proof another change is in the form of an older whiskey. Here, it''s an 8-year-old rye whiskey, sourced from an unspecified location.', FALSE, '2025-02-28', 'Herbs & Spices', 8, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/af7f19e0-bd8d-0133-8b0b-2a50787f104f/hochstadters_slow_low_100_proof_rock_rye_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100887, 'Automatic Jones Rock & Rye', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Automatic Jones Rock & Rye is produced by The Family Jones Spirits House in Denver, Colorado. It''s made from a base of straight rye whiskey and is infused with a combination of dried fruits and citrus peels, warming spices, and rock candy syrup. Automatic Jones Rock & Rye is produced by The Family Jones Spirits House in Denver, Colorado. It''s made from a base of straight rye whiskey and is infused with a combination of dried fruits and citrus peels, warming spices, and rock candy syrup. It''s bottled at 80 proof.', FALSE, '2025-02-17', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/dc564d30-101e-0139-1430-3e4eed358b50/rocknrye_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100613, 'Del Professore Aperitvo', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 15, 'Del Professore is a line of liqueurs, vermouth and bitters born out of the Jerry Thomas Speakeasy bar in Rome, Italy. Now available stateside, this aperitivo is in the Mediterranean style found in the cafes of Italy in the 1950s. The flavors are centered around mandarin orange, lemon, gentian, and a secret spice mixture, with ingredients said to be mostly Italian in origin. . Del Professore is a line of liqueurs, vermouth and bitters born out of the Jerry Thomas Speakeasy bar in Rome, Italy. Now available stateside, this aperitivo is in the Mediterranean style found in the cafes of Italy in the 1950s. The flavors are centered around mandarin orange, lemon, gentian, and a secret spice mixture, with ingredients said to be mostly Italian in origin.', FALSE, '2025-01-31', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/e257e440-0c14-0139-1128-0654e3ff27ae/DelProfessoreAperitvo_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101074, 'Caffè Borghetti Espresso Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 25, 'Caffè Borghetti Espresso Liqueur is based on an 1860s recipe created by cafè owner, Ugo Borghetti. It''s made with real Italian espresso made from Arabica and Robusta coffee beans, in addition to sugar and alcohol. Bottled at 25% ABV. . Caffè Borghetti Espresso Liqueur is based on an 1860s recipe created by cafè owner, Ugo Borghetti. It''s made with real Italian espresso made from Arabica and Robusta coffee beans, in addition to sugar and alcohol. Bottled at 25% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-02-07', 'Coffee', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/cd8cadd0-c1e3-0137-16e9-060fdf3dd4b6/caffe_borghetti_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101134, 'Copper & Kings Destillaré Intense Café', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 45, 'Introduced to its line of Desillaré liqueurs in 2019, Copper & Kings Destillaré Intense Café is made by adding cold brew Arabica coffee to a barrel filled with the distillery’s signature American Brandy. The blend of coffee and brandy is allowed to aged for an additional six to nine months, during which time additional vanilla beans, cardamom pods and coffee beans are also added to the barrel. Introduced to its line of Desillaré liqueurs in 2019, Copper & Kings Destillaré Intense Café is made by adding cold brew Arabica coffee to a barrel filled with the distillery’s signature American Brandy. The blend of coffee and brandy is allowed to aged for an additional six to nine months, during which time additional vanilla beans, cardamom pods and coffee beans are also added to the barrel. The liqueur is then diluted with additional cold brew coffee and sweetened with honey before being bottled at 90 proof.', FALSE, '2025-01-03', 'Coffee', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/c7fb5930-60ba-0137-2414-1e8cbf518b70/destillare_intense_cafe_liqueur_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100095, 'Casa D''Aristi Huana Mayan Liqueur', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Mexico', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 30, 'Made in Mexico’s Yucatan Peninsula, Huana (wa-nah) liqueur is flavored with Guanabana (aka soursop) fruits that resemble spiky green pears and have white flesh. The fruit is said to taste like a cross between strawberries and pineapple. Made in Mexico’s Yucatan Peninsula, Huana (wa-nah) liqueur is flavored with Guanabana (aka soursop) fruits that resemble spiky green pears and have white flesh. The fruit is said to taste like a cross between strawberries and pineapple. This rum-based fruit liqueur is bottled at 30% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-02-24', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/1e647910-5fe2-0137-e3ac-56e1dfb18f41/huana_mayan_liqueur_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100658, 'Cardinal Spirits Nocino', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Indiana''s Cardinal Spirits makes its nocino along traditional lines, researching old Italian recipes and methodology. They harvest green walnuts in midsummer, and steep them in alcohol for several months, in this case using their own vodka made from grapes. Indiana''s Cardinal Spirits makes its nocino along traditional lines, researching old Italian recipes and methodology. They harvest green walnuts in midsummer, and steep them in alcohol for several months, in this case using their own vodka made from grapes. Cinnamon and spices are added to the mixture as well, along with maple syrup from nearby Burton''s Maplewood Farm.', FALSE, '2025-01-02', 'Nut', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/f3c192c0-13d5-0137-0e9e-4af49495d734/cardinal_spirits_nocino_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101315, 'Amaro Lucano', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 30, 'Lucano Amaro is made in the town of Pisticci Scalo in Basilicata, Italy. It is made from more than 30 herbs and spices some of which are disclosed. They include: angelica root, bitter aloe, bitter orange, blessed thistle, clary sage, elderberry, gentian, musk yarrow, ruta, and woodworm. The company was founded in 1894 by Pasquale Vera and is now run by his grandson, his namesake, and his family. Lucano Amaro is made in the town of Pisticci Scalo in Basilicata, Italy. It is made from more than 30 herbs and spices some of which are disclosed. They include: angelica root, bitter aloe, bitter orange, blessed thistle, clary sage, elderberry, gentian, musk yarrow, ruta, and woodworm. The company was founded in 1894 by Pasquale Vera and is now run by his grandson, his namesake, and his family.', FALSE, '2025-01-05', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/b1337190-c1ee-0136-3e63-62ce6747e279/amaro_lucano_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100700, 'Reilly''s Rock & Rye Ginger Whiskey', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 33, 'Ginger was considered a powerful curative in the early 1900s, and was commonly found mixed with rye whiskey and sweetened with rock candy for a concoction found at many bars called "Rock and Rye." Post Prohibition it was relegated to a dusty jar kept behind the bar for old timers, but has recently found a resurgence. Reilly''s selected the rye whiskey (mash bill 51% rye, 45% corn, 4% malted barley) with Master Blender Dave Pickerell and infused it with ginger and spices for this updated interpretation. . Ginger was considered a powerful curative in the early 1900s, and was commonly found mixed with rye whiskey and sweetened with rock candy for a concoction found at many bars called "Rock and Rye." Post Prohibition it was relegated to a dusty jar kept behind the bar for old timers, but has recently found a resurgence. Reilly''s selected the rye whiskey (mash bill 51% rye, 45% corn, 4% malted barley) with Master Blender Dave Pickerell and infused it with ginger and spices for this updated interpretation.', FALSE, '2025-01-05', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/68f49a40-e607-0133-0554-66385cf1928e/reillys_rock_and_rye_ginger_whiskey_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100869, 'Amante 1530 Aperitivo Amaro', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 15, 'Amante 1530 is an Italian amaro made in Rome that is designed to have less sugar and a more subtle bitter finish than other amaro offerings on the market. Famed oenologist Riccardo Cotarella created and produced the product. Investors in the brand include English musician and actor Sting & his wife Trudie Styler among others. Amante 1530 launched in fall 2023 at select retailers, restaurants, and bars in New York with California and Florida to follow. (SRP $34.99). Amante 1530 is an Italian amaro made in Rome that is designed to have less sugar and a more subtle bitter finish than other amaro offerings on the market. Famed oenologist Riccardo Cotarella created and produced the product. Investors in the brand include English musician and actor Sting & his wife Trudie Styler among others. Amante 1530 launched in fall 2023 at select retailers, restaurants, and bars in New York with California and Florida to follow. (SRP $34.99)', FALSE, '2025-01-24', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/d10839c0-4089-013c-9a9a-4a51dbf2ecd6/amante-1530_original-1695963378.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100325, 'Amaro Meletti', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 32, 'Meletti Amaro is produced by a family-owned and operated company located in Le Marche. Most of the ingredients used are sourced from the region from growers who work exclusively with the brand. Known botanicals include anise, clove, gentian, orange peel, saffron, and violet flower. The method of cold-extraction known as percolation is the method for obtaining flavors and the neutral spirit base is a blend of molasses and beetroot. Meletti Amaro is produced by a family-owned and operated company located in Le Marche. Most of the ingredients used are sourced from the region from growers who work exclusively with the brand. Known botanicals include anise, clove, gentian, orange peel, saffron, and violet flower. The method of cold-extraction known as percolation is the method for obtaining flavors and the neutral spirit base is a blend of molasses and beetroot. Water and sugar are added as well.', FALSE, '2025-01-29', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/b2e70470-c1ef-0136-3e65-62ce6747e279/meletti_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100923, 'Green Hat Summer Cup', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 34, '“Cups” are a popular English tradition of combining gin with a variety of extra botanicals, herbs, spices, fruit, and some sort of sweetener. By far the market leader is Pimm’s, but the craft gin boom in America and abroad has ushered in a handful of competitors. Cue Washington DC’s Green Hat gin and their Summer Cup. The gin base is the distillery’s navy-strength gin which is combined with DC’s local Capitoline White Vermouth among a slew of other flavorful components. “Cups” are a popular English tradition of combining gin with a variety of extra botanicals, herbs, spices, fruit, and some sort of sweetener. By far the market leader is Pimm’s, but the craft gin boom in America and abroad has ushered in a handful of competitors. Cue Washington DC’s Green Hat gin and their Summer Cup. The gin base is the distillery’s navy-strength gin which is combined with DC’s local Capitoline White Vermouth among a slew of other flavorful components. The traditional way to enjoy is with lemon-lime soda or ginger ale.', FALSE, '2025-01-18', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/b0ae8a50-c6ef-0134-4f0e-1eba386d11de/green_hat_summer_cup_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100911, 'Mozart Pumpkin Spice Chocolate Liqueur', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Austria', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 17, 'Mozart Distillerie produces chocolate liqueurs in Salzburg, Austria — birthplace of composer Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart. This Pumpkin Spice expression is a fall seasonal release made with milk chocolate, caramel, natural pumpkin juice, cinnamon, clove and a hint of vanilla. It''s gluten free and bottled at 17% ABV. (SRP $29. Mozart Distillerie produces chocolate liqueurs in Salzburg, Austria — birthplace of composer Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart. This Pumpkin Spice expression is a fall seasonal release made with milk chocolate, caramel, natural pumpkin juice, cinnamon, clove and a hint of vanilla. It''s gluten free and bottled at 17% ABV. (SRP $29.99 per 750ml)', FALSE, '2025-02-13', 'Chocolate', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/ff305050-1b3c-0139-72f9-22742469456e/mozard_pumpkin_spice_original-1688675864.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101471, 'Don Ciccio & Figli Amaro Tonico Ferro-Kina', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 20, 'Don Ciccio & Figli Amaro Tonico Ferro-Kina is the first American made Iron Amaro. "Ferro" is Italian for "iron". Ferro-China is an amaro created in the late 19th century and included cinchona bark roasted on iron plates. Don Ciccio macerates their proprietary botanical blend in terra cotta amphoras. Bitter lemon, china calisaya, gentian lutea and bitter lemon are highlighted in this amaro. . Don Ciccio & Figli Amaro Tonico Ferro-Kina is the first American made Iron Amaro. "Ferro" is Italian for "iron". Ferro-China is an amaro created in the late 19th century and included cinchona bark roasted on iron plates. Don Ciccio macerates their proprietary botanical blend in terra cotta amphoras. Bitter lemon, china calisaya, gentian lutea and bitter lemon are highlighted in this amaro.', FALSE, '2025-02-12', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/7b1537c0-e9e4-0136-3c6c-62a8e2797a14/amaro_tocino_ferro_kina_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101151, 'Don Ciccio & Figli Cerasum Aperitivo', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 23, 'Cerasum is based on a traditional Italian recipe from 1906, respecting the original product from the Don Ciccio & Figli distillery, which produced liqueurs on Italy’s Amalfi Coast for nearly a century. Today, this recipe is being resurrected stateside by fourth generation family owner Francesco Amodeo who opened the Washington, D.C. distillery in 2012. It is based on an infusion of three different kinds of cherries, sakura blossoms, and 10 selected herbs & roots. . Cerasum is based on a traditional Italian recipe from 1906, respecting the original product from the Don Ciccio & Figli distillery, which produced liqueurs on Italy’s Amalfi Coast for nearly a century. Today, this recipe is being resurrected stateside by fourth generation family owner Francesco Amodeo who opened the Washington, D.C. distillery in 2012. It is based on an infusion of three different kinds of cherries, sakura blossoms, and 10 selected herbs & roots.', FALSE, '2025-02-25', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/8c920870-d96f-0136-447d-5acb4fe050d7/don_ciccio_and_figli_cerasum_aperitivo_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100284, 'Jack Daniel''s Tennessee Fire', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 35, 'Jack Daniel''s Tennessee Fire was released countrywide in March 2015 after a brief three state limited release. It is made from a blend of Jack Daniel''s Old No. Jack Daniel''s Tennessee Fire was released countrywide in March 2015 after a brief three state limited release. It is made from a blend of Jack Daniel''s Old No. 7 Tennessee Whiskey and Jack''s original cinnamon liqueur.', FALSE, '2025-01-22', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/db02f9e5-0e8d-4ff0-9c67-0a393af06f37/jack_daniels_tennessee_fire_new_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100727, 'Roulaison Amer Herbal Rum Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 41.6, 'New Orleans rum producer Roulaison Distilling launched at the end of 2016—Roulaison is the French-Creole term used for the sugar cane harvest. The distillery focuses on a pre-industrial style of rum, using pot stills and small batches. They also use 100% Louisiana molasses. Amer is a high-proof herbal rum liqueur, billed as more of a counterpoint to spiced rums, made with two dozen herbs and raw Louisiana sugar. New Orleans rum producer Roulaison Distilling launched at the end of 2016—Roulaison is the French-Creole term used for the sugar cane harvest. The distillery focuses on a pre-industrial style of rum, using pot stills and small batches. They also use 100% Louisiana molasses. Amer is a high-proof herbal rum liqueur, billed as more of a counterpoint to spiced rums, made with two dozen herbs and raw Louisiana sugar.', FALSE, '2025-01-02', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/8b039290-5031-0137-0424-02903339ac61/roulaison_amer_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100831, 'RumChata', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 13.75, 'RumChata is a liqueur made with Caribbean rum and dairy cream from Wisconsin. Cinnamon, vanilla, and sugar are also used. It is based on Horchata, a Latin American beverage made from rice, sugar, vanilla, and other spices. . RumChata is a liqueur made with Caribbean rum and dairy cream from Wisconsin. Cinnamon, vanilla, and sugar are also used. It is based on Horchata, a Latin American beverage made from rice, sugar, vanilla, and other spices.', FALSE, '2025-01-02', 'Cream', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/afcda920-dd86-0136-46e8-524561623431/rumchata_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101533, 'Villon Liqueur', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Villon is a blended spirit which cuts across categories. It''s made from a base of VSOP and XO Cognacs, as well as spirits distilled from French wheat, and natural flavors. Villon is a blended spirit which cuts across categories. It''s made from a base of VSOP and XO Cognacs, as well as spirits distilled from French wheat, and natural flavors. The brand is named for 15th century French poet François Villon, whom they say they share a renegade streak with, and is technically bottled as a liqueur.', FALSE, '2025-01-19', 'Other', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/979f7100-d48e-0139-c97f-163e35644993/villon_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100945, 'Douglas & Todd Bourbon Cream', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 15, 'Douglas & Todd Bourbon Cream starts with the brand''s Small Batch Bourbon which is aged for a minimum of 4 years. Vanilla bean flavors and cream sourced from Midwestern farms are used in the production of this liqueur. Douglas & Todd Bourbon Cream starts with the brand''s Small Batch Bourbon which is aged for a minimum of 4 years. Vanilla bean flavors and cream sourced from Midwestern farms are used in the production of this liqueur. Bottled at 30 proof, this cream liqueur is limited edition release which launched in fall 2020.', FALSE, '2025-02-24', 'Cream', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/e89d7810-e635-0138-4905-22b01fb204fb/douglas_todd_bourbon_cream_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101193, 'Gran Gala Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Canada', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Gran Gala is a clear orange liqueur made from "VSOP" Italian brandy and three varieties of oranges. This brand is owned by the Sazerac Company. Gran Gala is a clear orange liqueur made from "VSOP" Italian brandy and three varieties of oranges. This brand is owned by the Sazerac Company.', FALSE, '2025-01-07', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/0d0bf680-d5b4-0136-4084-3e28faf1a0ff/gran_gala_liqueur_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100358, 'Baileys Original Irish Cream', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Ireland', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 17, 'First introduced in 1974, Baileys Original Irish Cream is made from Irish whiskey, Irish cream, spirit, and chocolate. This brand is currently owned by Diageo and there are many other flavors in the Baileys portfolio including vegan and gluten free versions. Bottled at 17% ABV in Ireland. . First introduced in 1974, Baileys Original Irish Cream is made from Irish whiskey, Irish cream, spirit, and chocolate. This brand is currently owned by Diageo and there are many other flavors in the Baileys portfolio including vegan and gluten free versions. Bottled at 17% ABV in Ireland.', FALSE, '2025-02-01', 'Cream', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/6cb02f80-d5ac-0136-d4d8-123305d01a9a/baileys_original_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100771, 'Kahlúa', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Mexico', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 20, 'Kahlúa is a coffee flavored liqueur produced in Mexico City. Arabica coffee beans are harvested, dried, and roasted before they are ground. Coffee is brewed then added to sugarcane spirit (along with vanilla and caramel coloring). Kahlúa was created in Mexico in 1936 and first introduced to the US in 1940. It is an essential ingredient in a Black Russian, White Russian, and Mudslide cocktails among many others. Bottled at 20% ABV, except in Ohio for some reason where it is bottled at 21. Kahlúa is a coffee flavored liqueur produced in Mexico City. Arabica coffee beans are harvested, dried, and roasted before they are ground. Coffee is brewed then added to sugarcane spirit (along with vanilla and caramel coloring). Kahlúa was created in Mexico in 1936 and first introduced to the US in 1940. It is an essential ingredient in a Black Russian, White Russian, and Mudslide cocktails among many others. Bottled at 20% ABV, except in Ohio for some reason where it is bottled at 21.5% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-01-26', 'Coffee', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/8455e920-d5b9-0136-4085-3e28faf1a0ff/kahlua_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100662, 'Paladin Agricanto Liqueur', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 25, 'Made in the Italian region of Veneto, Agricanto Liqueur is made at Cantine Paladin. It’s intended to channel the flavors and subtleties of wine, specifically that made of from the red Raboso grape. The base of the liqueur is made up of Paladin Estate Raboso wine, grappa, and spice extracts. To that, cherry juice, almond, and sugar are added. Made in the Italian region of Veneto, Agricanto Liqueur is made at Cantine Paladin. It’s intended to channel the flavors and subtleties of wine, specifically that made of from the red Raboso grape. The base of the liqueur is made up of Paladin Estate Raboso wine, grappa, and spice extracts. To that, cherry juice, almond, and sugar are added. Bottled at 50 proof.', FALSE, '2025-02-01', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/7d07e580-5fee-0137-ea63-1aa8c474f3d0/agricanto_paladin_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100512, 'Tuaca', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Canada', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 35, 'Tuaca is a liqueur made from Italian brandy, citrus, and vanilla. The name is derived from the last names of the two brothers-in-law, Gaetano Tuoni and Giorgia Canepa, who in the 1930s recreated a recipe from the Renaissance period for this liqueur. The product was first introduced to the US in the 1950s. Tuaca is now owned by Sazerac which completed the purchase of the brand from Brown-Forman in March 2016. Sazerac has reformulated the recipe to utilize Italian brandy replacing the California brandy which Brown-Forman used. . Tuaca is a liqueur made from Italian brandy, citrus, and vanilla. The name is derived from the last names of the two brothers-in-law, Gaetano Tuoni and Giorgia Canepa, who in the 1930s recreated a recipe from the Renaissance period for this liqueur. The product was first introduced to the US in the 1950s. Tuaca is now owned by Sazerac which completed the purchase of the brand from Brown-Forman in March 2016. Sazerac has reformulated the recipe to utilize Italian brandy replacing the California brandy which Brown-Forman used.', FALSE, '2025-01-29', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/b40f29c0-dd89-0136-9b23-561f8738e82c/tuaca_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100275, 'Jim Beam Honey', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 35, 'Jim Beam Honey is made with real honey and natural flavors. It is infused with Kentucky straight bourbon. Jim Beam Honey is made with real honey and natural flavors. It is infused with Kentucky straight bourbon. Bottled at 70 proof.', FALSE, '2025-01-16', 'Other', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/ed6c6f60-714e-0133-02c9-3ebda71fe287/jim_beam_honey_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100955, 'Southern Comfort Original', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 35, 'Southern Comfort was first created by M.W. Heron in 1874. Though originally made with a whiskey base, for many years the spirit was omitted from the recipe. But after the Sazerac Company acquired the brand in 2016, the 70-proof liqueur returned to its roots. Now, Southern Comfort is made from an undisclosed blend of Sazerac-owned whiskeys and accented with fruit and spice flavors. Southern Comfort was first created by M.W. Heron in 1874. Though originally made with a whiskey base, for many years the spirit was omitted from the recipe. But after the Sazerac Company acquired the brand in 2016, the 70-proof liqueur returned to its roots. Now, Southern Comfort is made from an undisclosed blend of Sazerac-owned whiskeys and accented with fruit and spice flavors. Notably, the liqueur was beloved by rock and roll legend Janis Joplin at the height of her career in the 1960s.', FALSE, '2025-01-23', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/7ac68ca0-e2f8-0136-81f3-1eddfb7eb518/southern_comfort_original_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
