(100917, 'Fleur Charmante', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 34, 'Fleur Charmante, which means “charming flower”, is a liqueur made in the Saint Sauvant in the Saintonge area of France. Its base spirit is macerated in a combination of blackcurrant, raspberry and cherry fruits along with essences of violet, lavender, and jasmine. It is bottled at 34% ABV, and available as of July, 2021. . Fleur Charmante, which means “charming flower”, is a liqueur made in the Saint Sauvant in the Saintonge area of France. Its base spirit is macerated in a combination of blackcurrant, raspberry and cherry fruits along with essences of violet, lavender, and jasmine. It is bottled at 34% ABV, and available as of July, 2021.', FALSE, '2025-01-31', 'Floral', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/01e50120-c7d2-0139-5bd9-16d2eb3053a8/fleurcharmante_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
