(101251, 'Tattersall Amaro', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 30, 'Tattersall Distilling Co. is located in northeast Minneapolis and produces over 30 different spirits ranging from vodka, rum, gin, and various liqueurs and ready to drink offerings. Their amaro is flavored with various roots and barks as well as macerated citrus. It''s bottled at 30% ABV. Tattersall Distilling Co. is located in northeast Minneapolis and produces over 30 different spirits ranging from vodka, rum, gin, and various liqueurs and ready to drink offerings. Their amaro is flavored with various roots and barks as well as macerated citrus. It''s bottled at 30% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-01-13', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/8a249bd0-10bd-0139-1bf0-067fa9b21d8b/tattersall_amaro_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100310, 'Revolution Spirits Amico Amaro', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 25, 'Revolution Spirits in Austin, Texas introduced Amico Amaro to their portfolio in 2017. This amaro, translated to "bitter friend", is made in the style of Campari or Aperol with 12 botanicals which they fully disclose. Hibiscus, sumac, cedar, orange peel, gentian root, cinchona bark, Apollo hops, witch hazel leaf, blessed thistle, damiana, cranberry and fennel are used here. This bottling marks the first amaro to be released in the state of Texas. Revolution Spirits in Austin, Texas introduced Amico Amaro to their portfolio in 2017. This amaro, translated to "bitter friend", is made in the style of Campari or Aperol with 12 botanicals which they fully disclose. Hibiscus, sumac, cedar, orange peel, gentian root, cinchona bark, Apollo hops, witch hazel leaf, blessed thistle, damiana, cranberry and fennel are used here. This bottling marks the first amaro to be released in the state of Texas.', FALSE, '2025-02-22', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/6b32f320-10aa-0139-6cce-1e7c6d6df89d/amico_amaro_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100669, 'Bully Boy Amaro', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 29, 'Bully Boy Amaro is made using a base of neutral grain spirit and rum along with 26 botanicals. Some of these botanicals include coriander, grapefruit peel, fig, orange blossom, orange peel, rhubarb root, Szechuan peppercorn and hops (Amarillo, Cascade, Citra, and Galaxy). Bully Boy Amaro is made using a base of neutral grain spirit and rum along with 26 botanicals. Some of these botanicals include coriander, grapefruit peel, fig, orange blossom, orange peel, rhubarb root, Szechuan peppercorn and hops (Amarillo, Cascade, Citra, and Galaxy). It''s bottled at 58 proof.', FALSE, '2025-01-12', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/77874970-101c-0139-142f-3e4eed358b50/bully_boy_amaro_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100397, 'La Boîte American Amaro', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 20, 'La Boîte American Amaro is a bitter liqueur made in collaboration with NYC-based spice store La Boîte and Indiana-based craft distillery Cardinal Spirits. La Boîte founder and spice master Lior Lev Sercarz crafted the spice blend for the amaro which includes star anise, licorice, orange, and green cardamom. La Boîte American Amaro is a bitter liqueur made in collaboration with NYC-based spice store La Boîte and Indiana-based craft distillery Cardinal Spirits. La Boîte founder and spice master Lior Lev Sercarz crafted the spice blend for the amaro which includes star anise, licorice, orange, and green cardamom.', FALSE, '2025-01-01', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/b27b1210-1019-0139-11ec-0654e3ff27ae/la_boite_amaro_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
