(101397, 'Carpano Botanic Bitter', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 25, 'This bitter aperitivo from Carpano is made with 10 aromatic herbs. These include cinchona, saffron, gentian, bitter orange peel, fresh orange green peel, myrrh, rhubarb, wormwood, sandal, and zedoaria. This bitter aperitivo from Carpano is made with 10 aromatic herbs. These include cinchona, saffron, gentian, bitter orange peel, fresh orange green peel, myrrh, rhubarb, wormwood, sandal, and zedoaria. It is bottled at 25% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-02-13', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/a69801c0-c024-0138-6dc3-221a502822fb/carpano_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100703, 'Angostura Cocoa Bitters', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Trinidad & Tobago', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 48, 'Angostura Cocoa Bitters is made with Trinitario cocoa nibs grown on the islands of Trinidad & Tobago among other botanicals. This is just the third bitters for the brand following their Orange Bitters launch in 2007. Angostura Cocoa Bitters debuted in the US in August 2020. . Angostura Cocoa Bitters is made with Trinitario cocoa nibs grown on the islands of Trinidad & Tobago among other botanicals. This is just the third bitters for the brand following their Orange Bitters launch in 2007. Angostura Cocoa Bitters debuted in the US in August 2020.', FALSE, '2025-02-26', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/beec64c0-bd54-0138-a129-2e192f3aace1/angostura_cocoa_bitters_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101155, 'Cardenal Mendoza Angêlus Liqueur', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Spain', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 40, 'Cardenal Mendoza Angêlus Liqueur is made using the brand''s own Spanish brandy as its base. It is flavored with Seville oranges, lemons from Valencia, cardamom, and cloves. After maceration, the flavored brandy is then placed into sherry-seasoned butts to age. This Spanish liqueur is bottled at 40% ABV. Cardenal Mendoza Angêlus Liqueur is made using the brand''s own Spanish brandy as its base. It is flavored with Seville oranges, lemons from Valencia, cardamom, and cloves. After maceration, the flavored brandy is then placed into sherry-seasoned butts to age. This Spanish liqueur is bottled at 40% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-02-03', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/029c6180-b58d-0138-9fe6-2e192f3aace1/cardenal_mendoza_angelus_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
