(100334, 'Élixir Végétal de la Grande-Chartreuse', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 69, 'Élixir Végétal de la Grande-Chartreuse has been made by the Chartreuse monks since 1764 according to instructions they received by the Duc d''Estrées in 1605. It is made from 130 medicinal and aromatic plants and flowers. It is sold in a wooden box to protect the bottle from the light. Serving recommendations include adding a few drops to a sugar cube or to serve in sugared water. Note: Sold in 100ml sized bottles and not available in the US. . Élixir Végétal de la Grande-Chartreuse has been made by the Chartreuse monks since 1764 according to instructions they received by the Duc d''Estrées in 1605. It is made from 130 medicinal and aromatic plants and flowers. It is sold in a wooden box to protect the bottle from the light. Serving recommendations include adding a few drops to a sugar cube or to serve in sugared water. Note: Sold in 100ml sized bottles and not available in the US.', FALSE, '2025-01-13', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/47f64190-e1a4-0137-3096-5a39ab607e99/elixir_vegetal_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
