(101528, 'Jeppson''s Malört', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 35, 'This intensely bitter wormwood liqueur was first made during Prohibition in Chicago by Carl Jeppson as a bäskbrännvin, a Swedish influenced curative digestif, and has been in legal existence since 1933. It was made and discontinued at several distilleries over the years, and is now available through CH Distillery in its home town of Chicago. It is bottled at 70 proof. . This intensely bitter wormwood liqueur was first made during Prohibition in Chicago by Carl Jeppson as a bäskbrännvin, a Swedish influenced curative digestif, and has been in legal existence since 1933. It was made and discontinued at several distilleries over the years, and is now available through CH Distillery in its home town of Chicago. It is bottled at 70 proof.', FALSE, '2025-02-10', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/7108fce0-7d85-0137-f8e1-3691941de48a/jeppsonsmalort_original-1661808399.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100684, 'Yuzuri Yuzu Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Japan', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 30, 'Yuzuri Yuzu Liqueur is a citrus liqueur made from Japanese yuzu fruit which is harvested once a year in the late fall. The base spirit is made from 100% rice and groundwater from the island of Kyushu. Sugar beets and Australian sugarcane are added to the yuzu to balance the tartness of the fruit. Bottled at 60 proof. Yuzuri Yuzu Liqueur is a citrus liqueur made from Japanese yuzu fruit which is harvested once a year in the late fall. The base spirit is made from 100% rice and groundwater from the island of Kyushu. Sugar beets and Australian sugarcane are added to the yuzu to balance the tartness of the fruit. Bottled at 60 proof.', FALSE, '2025-01-10', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/56b79bd0-7b4e-0137-7844-1e39d9abc8e0/yuzuri_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100993, 'Galliano l''Aperitivo', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 24, 'Galliano l''Aperitivo is a bright red bitter liqueur made using a variety of infusions using Mediterranean citrus fruits including oranges, bergamots, bitter oranges, chinottos, tangerines, and grapefruit. Additionally, a touch of Galliano l''Autentico--the brand''s classic herbal liqueur featuring 30 herbs, spices, and plant extracts-- is added. Featured botanicals include anise, juniper, cardamom, sandalwood, sage, lavender, peppermint, cinnamon, and vanilla. . Galliano l''Aperitivo is a bright red bitter liqueur made using a variety of infusions using Mediterranean citrus fruits including oranges, bergamots, bitter oranges, chinottos, tangerines, and grapefruit. Additionally, a touch of Galliano l''Autentico--the brand''s classic herbal liqueur featuring 30 herbs, spices, and plant extracts-- is added. Featured botanicals include anise, juniper, cardamom, sandalwood, sage, lavender, peppermint, cinnamon, and vanilla.', FALSE, '2025-02-06', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/3bc36450-790f-0137-a7bf-46a71b3af8ab/galliano_l_aperitivo_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101369, 'Select Aperitivo Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 17.5, 'Select Aperitivo is made using 30 botanicals with juniper berries and rhubarb root being the standouts. The red bittersweet liqueur was founded in 1920 and celebrated throughout Venice. The Original Venetian Spritz recipe calls for 3 parts Prosecco, 2 parts Select Aperitivo, and 1 part soda and lots of ice. Garnish with a skewered green olive. Select Aperitivo is made using 30 botanicals with juniper berries and rhubarb root being the standouts. The red bittersweet liqueur was founded in 1920 and celebrated throughout Venice. The Original Venetian Spritz recipe calls for 3 parts Prosecco, 2 parts Select Aperitivo, and 1 part soda and lots of ice. Garnish with a skewered green olive.', FALSE, '2025-01-03', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/8b412f80-790a-0137-7e71-1abd9ac5d9db/select_aperitivo_liqueur_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100523, 'Peychaud''s Aperitivo', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 11, 'Peychaud''s Aperitivo was launched in 2016 by its parent company, Sazerac, which also produces the classic Peychaud''s Bitters. This bright red bitter liqueur is bottled at 22 proof. Peychaud''s Aperitivo was launched in 2016 by its parent company, Sazerac, which also produces the classic Peychaud''s Bitters. This bright red bitter liqueur is bottled at 22 proof.', FALSE, '2025-01-03', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/363fd120-7901-0137-7e6e-1abd9ac5d9db/peychauds_aperitivo_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101388, 'Meletti 1870 Bitter Aperitivo', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 25, 'Meletti 1870 Bitter Aperitivo is made with a blend of three distillates: a sweet orange, a bitter orange, and a spice and herb infusion. In addition to the citrus, disclosed botanicals include gentian, coriander, clove, and cinnamon. The bitter bright red liqueur gets its name from the year the Silvio Meletti Company was founded. . Meletti 1870 Bitter Aperitivo is made with a blend of three distillates: a sweet orange, a bitter orange, and a spice and herb infusion. In addition to the citrus, disclosed botanicals include gentian, coriander, clove, and cinnamon. The bitter bright red liqueur gets its name from the year the Silvio Meletti Company was founded.', FALSE, '2025-02-25', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/150ee7e0-78fe-0137-4920-765bda5edd8a/meletti_1870_bitter_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101464, 'Luxardo Bitter Rosso', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 25, 'Luxardo Bitter Rosso is a red bitter liqueur from the Italian brand, best known for its Maraschino Liqueur. The brand''s Bitter Rosso is made from an infusion of herbs, spices, and citrus fruits such as mint, marjoram, thyme, and bitter orange. Vegan friendly and Kosher certified. . Luxardo Bitter Rosso is a red bitter liqueur from the Italian brand, best known for its Maraschino Liqueur. The brand''s Bitter Rosso is made from an infusion of herbs, spices, and citrus fruits such as mint, marjoram, thyme, and bitter orange. Vegan friendly and Kosher certified.', FALSE, '2025-02-09', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/18431f50-78fa-0137-491e-765bda5edd8a/luxardo_bitter_rosso_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100300, 'Fernet-Branca Menta', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Italy', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 30, 'Fernet-Branca Menta is a mint variation of Fernet-Branca. It was created in the 1960''s when the brand recognized the growing practice of adding mint syrup to Fernet-Branca. Fernet-Branca Menta is a mint variation of Fernet-Branca. It was created in the 1960''s when the brand recognized the growing practice of adding mint syrup to Fernet-Branca. It is based on the same proprietary recipe as Fernet-Branca, and is bottled at 30% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-02-20', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/2ed02550-7688-0137-3357-4edf11e22f8d/branca_menta_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
