(101249, 'Clear Creek Cherry Liqueur', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 19.01, 'Clear Creek Cherry Liqueur is made with dark, sweet cherries from the cherry orchards in the Columbia River Gorge near The Dalles, Oregon. Bottled at 38. Clear Creek Cherry Liqueur is made with dark, sweet cherries from the cherry orchards in the Columbia River Gorge near The Dalles, Oregon. Bottled at 38.02% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-01-29', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/979df130-50cf-0137-7469-3694c9b94e1d/clear_creek_cherry_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101016, 'Mathilde Framboise Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 18, 'Mathilde Framboise Liqueur is made with three types of raspberries: Lloyd George from Scotland and Rose de Plombières and Violette de Boux, both from Burgundy. These raspberries are pressed and infused in alcohol for a time. Then the berry spirit passes through a sieve before sugar and water is added. No preservatives or stabilizers are added. Bottled at 18% ABV. . Mathilde Framboise Liqueur is made with three types of raspberries: Lloyd George from Scotland and Rose de Plombières and Violette de Boux, both from Burgundy. These raspberries are pressed and infused in alcohol for a time. Then the berry spirit passes through a sieve before sugar and water is added. No preservatives or stabilizers are added. Bottled at 18% ABV.', FALSE, '2025-01-07', 'Fruit', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/e064d280-50c2-0137-1de4-3647b9f07964/mathilde_framboise_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101065, 'Crème Yvette', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'France', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 27.75, 'Crème Yvette is a berry and violet liqueur and was first produced and sold in the US around 1890. It ceased production around 1969, but was reintroduced in 2010 by Cooper Spirits. It is made with four berry fruits: mure (blackberry), framboise (raspberry), cassis (black currants), and fraise sauvage (wild strawberries). This is blended with dried violet petals from Provence. Honey and orange peel is also used. . Crème Yvette is a berry and violet liqueur and was first produced and sold in the US around 1890. It ceased production around 1969, but was reintroduced in 2010 by Cooper Spirits. It is made with four berry fruits: mure (blackberry), framboise (raspberry), cassis (black currants), and fraise sauvage (wild strawberries). This is blended with dried violet petals from Provence. Honey and orange peel is also used.', FALSE, '2025-02-08', 'Floral', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/29adacb0-4c2c-0137-c9ed-162410bf8760/creme_yvette_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100572, 'The King''s Ginger Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Netherlands', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 41, 'The King''s Ginger Liqueur is made for Berry Bros & Rudd in Schiedam, Netherlands. To make, fresh ginger macerates in a neutral spirit for 4 weeks. Lemon oil distillate is then added to the ginger spirit. Sugar is added and the liqueur is bottled at 41% ABV. The liqueur is named The King''s Ginger as this was formulated for Berry Bros & Rudd in 1903 for King Edward VII. . The King''s Ginger Liqueur is made for Berry Bros & Rudd in Schiedam, Netherlands. To make, fresh ginger macerates in a neutral spirit for 4 weeks. Lemon oil distillate is then added to the ginger spirit. Sugar is added and the liqueur is bottled at 41% ABV. The liqueur is named The King''s Ginger as this was formulated for Berry Bros & Rudd in 1903 for King Edward VII.', FALSE, '2025-01-11', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/9a4df840-4c2b-0137-c9ec-162410bf8760/kings_ginger_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
