(100431, 'SŌMRUS Mango Cream Liqueur', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 13.5, 'SŌMRUS Mango Cream Liqueur is inspired by an Indian Mango Shake or Lassi. It is made with Alphonso mangoes known as the "king of the mangos" which are generally harvested in April and May. SŌMRUS Mango Cream Liqueur is inspired by an Indian Mango Shake or Lassi. It is made with Alphonso mangoes known as the "king of the mangos" which are generally harvested in April and May.', FALSE, '2025-01-10', 'Cream', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/4f2e3f80-1c49-0137-1ed9-321b71432c95/somrus_mango_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100616, 'The Bitter Truth Golden Falernum', 22, 'Original Bottling', 'Germany', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 18, 'The Bitter Truth Golden Falernum is a rum-based liqueur flavored with ginger, citrus fruits, almonds, and allspice among others. . The Bitter Truth Golden Falernum is a rum-based liqueur flavored with ginger, citrus fruits, almonds, and allspice among others.', FALSE, '2025-01-27', 'Other', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/9299fe90-1c46-0137-1ed7-321b71432c95/bitter_truth_golden_falernum_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100630, 'Watershed Barrel-Finished Nocino', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 25.2, 'Ohio-based Watershed Distillery first started making Nocino in 2014 after a local physician named Charlie convinced them to try his homemade version. Unripe black walnuts from Ohio are used in its creation along with sugar and spices. Released annually in small batches so ABV will vary. . Ohio-based Watershed Distillery first started making Nocino in 2014 after a local physician named Charlie convinced them to try his homemade version. Unripe black walnuts from Ohio are used in its creation along with sugar and spices. Released annually in small batches so ABV will vary.', FALSE, '2025-01-11', 'Nut', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/02a55480-1c5c-0137-67a4-1e32c900bc5d/watershed-barrel-finished-nocino_original-1700702156.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(100728, 'Chareau Aloe Liqueur', 21, 'Original Bottling', 'United States', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 25, 'Chareau Aloe Liqueur is made using California ingredients, organic when possible. In addition to aloe vera, ingredients of cucumber, lemon peel, muskmelon, spearmint are used to flavor the grape-based eau de vie. Sugar and California spring water are added as well. The name is an amalgamation of Arthur Emile Charron & Florence Marie Favreau, the great-grandparents of brand''s founder who moved to California where they were farmers. Chareau Aloe Liqueur is made using California ingredients, organic when possible. In addition to aloe vera, ingredients of cucumber, lemon peel, muskmelon, spearmint are used to flavor the grape-based eau de vie. Sugar and California spring water are added as well. The name is an amalgamation of Arthur Emile Charron & Florence Marie Favreau, the great-grandparents of brand''s founder who moved to California where they were farmers.', FALSE, '2025-02-25', 'Other', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/d772ad80-1c44-0137-678f-1e32c900bc5d/chareau_aloe_liqueur_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
(101003, 'Gran Classico Bitter Liqueur', 1, 'Original Bottling', 'Switzerland', 'Liqueurs & Bitters', 28, 'Gran Classico Bitter Liqueur is made using an original 1860s recipe made in Turin, Italy. Today, the Tempus Fugit brand makes it in Switzerland macerating 25 herbs and roots including wormwood, gentian, rhubarb, hyssop, and bitter orange peel among others. The maceration imparts an all-natural color to the bitter liqueur with no additional coloring needed. . Gran Classico Bitter Liqueur is made using an original 1860s recipe made in Turin, Italy. Today, the Tempus Fugit brand makes it in Switzerland macerating 25 herbs and roots including wormwood, gentian, rhubarb, hyssop, and bitter orange peel among others. The maceration imparts an all-natural color to the bitter liqueur with no additional coloring needed.', FALSE, '2025-02-13', 'Herbs & Spices', 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'https://ip-distiller.imgix.net/images/spirits/bc1cf960-1c37-0137-1ecf-321b71432c95/gran_classico_bitter_original.jpg?w=280&h=280&mark-w=70&mark-h=70&fit=crop&crop=right&mark-align=top,left&mark-pad=0&mark='),
